{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1101014-w-ta-the-house-canon-thread-what-s-true-at-your-table","id":1101014,"title":"[W:TA] The House Canon Thread - What's True at your Table?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-06-06T16:30:31-07:00","id":1101014,"title":"[W:TA] The House Canon Thread - What's True at your Table?","content":"What the title says.<br /> <br /> Everybody changes stuff about Werewolf canon for their games. They adjust the rules, adjust the tribal lore, and generally play around with the characters as well as storylines. So, share what's different at your tables and why.<br /> <br /> Maybe some of us will make adjustments to our own.<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-06T17:00:13-07:00","id":1101022,"title":"","content":"<u>CTPhipps changes</u><br /> <br /> <b>NPCs</b><br /> <br /> * Evan &quot;Heals the Past&quot; is a Child of Gaia because the Wendigo wouldn't accept a Caucasian child raised outside Native American culture. He fits in better there both in-universe and out of universe. Had be been born in Canada, there might have been more wiggle room but he's far from the only Caucasian Wendigo of the lineage around who was rejected by them.<br /> <br /> * Samuel Haight does exist as a werewolf serial killer scare legend and the first Skinwalker. Most of the stories about him being anything other than that is Nuwisha and Ragbash stories.<br /> <br /> <b>The Garou Nation</b><br /> <br /> * Garou cultural posturing is something which is a major issue of the society and just about everyone is guilty of lying, embellishment, propagandizing, or more regarding their history. This is something which seriously impacts anyone who wants to know the truth of Garou history.<br /> <br /> * The War of Rage wasn't caused by anything in particular but is the result of many grievances spreading to other packs before everyone was avenging someone else. Even those who sided with Fera got murdered by other Fera because they weren't guiltless either. A lot of Past Lives also egged their inheritors on.<br /> <br /> * Garou reincarnate despite what newer editions say.<br /> <br /> * Garou have an elaborate Braid system for styling their fur to let people know of their deeds. Ditto Tattoos.<br /> <br /> <b>Tribes</b><br /> <br /> * The Swords of Heimdall still exist in my games but are not Nazis as the Get find them a bunch of poseurs who lost their war. Instead, they're a group of Get of Fenris supremacists who believe they should rule the Garou Nation and are obsessed with the pure breed of their kinfolk. Rather than being horrified by this, the majority of Garou just think of them as Get of Fenris acting like wannabe Silver Fangs.<br /> <br /> * Shadow Lords are generally more popular than Silver Fangs as pack/sept leaders and work as politicians versus Medieval Lords. They don't rule the Garou nation because popularity is not how things are determined.<br /> <br /> * Bone Gnawers are considered honorless because they have no real code of ethics in how they achieve victory and are the best assassins among the Garou. They also have been known to make deals with vampires, use human weapons, break oaths, and generally do whatever it takes to survive--which has worked well for them.<br /> <br /> * The Bone Gnawers are originally casteless werewolves born from kinfolk breeding outside of accepted lineages. It worked out for them as well.<br /> <br /> * The Silent Striders killed Set and bound his spirit underneath Egypt. They're, thus, the first supernatural group to have killed an Antediluvian.<br /> <br /> * The Garou claim to have killed Baba Yaga themselves, whether it's true or not.<br /> <br /> <b>Spirits</b><br /> <br /> * Spirits are fundamentally somewhat alien and shaped by the perception of the viewer so their answers can never quite be trusted. A spirit viewed by a Glass Walker, Silver Fang, and Bone Gnawer of different cultures will often have very different appearances as well as answers. They also lie and play to their summoners' prejudices very often.<br /> <br /> * Garou have met Judeo-Christian-Islam demons ala Demon: The Fallen and both sides completely confuse the other before leading to fights (which the demons tend to lose but not badly as Garou spirit magic doesn't work on them well).<br /> <br /> <b>Pentex</b><br /> <br /> * The scary thing about Pentex is that a long time ago, a lot of their executives realized they didn't have to do ANYTHING but carry out business as usual to please their masters. As such, Pentex really runs like normal conglomerates for the most part with the occasional baby sacrifice or banes to gain specific boons or demonic investments. Sometimes, regular human businessmen exceed them in evil (and thus get recruited).<br /> <br /> * Endron Oil ceased operations in 2001 to coincide with the RL company of Enron's collapse. This was done with the help of Monkeywrenchers, Virtual Adepts, and (of all people) the Syndicate. Pentex has a number of small energy companies but it was a serious blow in their control over the world economy.<br /> <br /> * The Syndicate has purified itself of its Special Operations Division but ironically ended up allying itself with the Weaver's Shinzui Industries. This was done during the Housing Market Collapse and resulted in the New World Order putting a crimp on Syndicate plans. Pentex has since retaliated and are benefiting greatly from the current administration's polices.<br /> <br /> <b>Leeches</b><br /> <br /> * Territory disputes between Garou and vampires are more common in my universe. Garou often send a younger cub to go in, track down a vampire, and murder him as a rite of passage. Vampires often retaliate and try to identify Garou to eliminate. There's been more than a few wars over the years with a few genuine hot zones where Garou treat vampires as kill-on-sight like Mexico City and Milwaukee.<br /> <br /> Both sides know a good deal more about the other than in canon but neither really wants war and local truces often exist. At least in the context of, &quot;I'll kill you guys last. I have wyrmspawn to deal with.&quot;<br /> <br /> * The Sabbat pretty much fund themselves entirely from their section of Pentex because they can't afford anything else and don't spend any time managing their funds. Their ghoul families involved thus have more loyalty to Pentex than they do their masters, blood bonds be damned. Ironically, euro for euro, the Camarilla owns a far bigger share of Pentex businesses than the Sabbat does but only invested from afar as Pentex is an incredible stable set of conglomerates.<br /> <br /> The Pentex board keeps the Camarilla away because it's legitimately one of the organizations which could destroy them/take them over along with an uncorrupted syndicate.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 06-07-2017, 11:34 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-07T04:49:48-07:00","id":1101174,"title":"","content":"-World in general-<br /> <br /> WoD is not a nice place, less because the setting is dark, and more because centuries of supernatural influence have molded it to go into different routes than our world. However, this isn't all bad. Nature is much more vibrant and much more plentiful in WoD, thanks to garou and kinfolk efforts. Of course, the average joe won't get to experience this beauty as any plot of land that can be salvaged for territory by garou or any other changer, is guarded.<br /> <br /> There is no Pentex. Rather, the Wyrm's corruption can appear anywhere where corners were cut and where cheap labour was used. While there are stores that are tainted, there is no greater conspiracy behind it.<br /> <br /> The tribes<br /> <br /> Black Furies are dealing with a lot of questions on the nature of their chosen gender. While the tribe has always been open for transwomen, some of the tribe have argued that they must still defend womanity as Gaia defined it. Not helping is that there is a constant push and pull between the witches or the tribe, and those who don't want women put under such stereotypes.<br /> <br /> Bone Gnawers are survialists, they are the ones that on purpose take the hardest lands and the toughest kinfolk and live where others rarely dare to tread. Their take on survival still makes other tribes scoff, as Bone Gnawers rarely bother with grand displays of honour.<br /> <br /> Children of Gaia Elders have to try and figure out what to do about their youths, who lack the proper education and tribal unity to really even understand the Litany proper. They also have to push back a faction in their tribe that wants to rule the garou nation under the banner of one tribe.<br /> <br /> Fenrir generally stay the same, but I have tried to make sure each one mimics their native country better. Finnish fenrir are less norse and more animistic, American fenrir are trying to figure out their heritage vs their nationality HARD these days.<br /> <br /> Fianna still keep their metis mostly unrited and in servant positions in various wooded areas of their Caerns. But Unicorn and Stag have started conversations on fixing this, as family should not leave family to suffer.<br /> <br /> Glass Walkers have more lupus, thanks to people owning wolfdogs more. Of course this means that their lupus run around with only 3-4 Gnosis, and are housebroken, but they now have the wolf voice among them. Walkers also are enjoying the current trends of building things, cooking and such, yourself. Not to mention, new technology makes it easier to fight for Gaia now.<br /> <br /> Red Talons deal with humans suddenly giving wolves more land, more urbanized wolves and just general relaxing of the wolf-hate in some areas with bafflement. Especially when a lot of their cliath have grown more used to humans or have positive experiences of them. The Whelp's Compromise is now more openly accepted.<br /> <br /> Silver Fangs function like the houses of Westeros, barely noticing the other tribes in their constant inner bickerings. Things have gotten silly, though, as they can no longer recruit other tribes to their causes, much to their annoyance.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-08T06:43:08-07:00","id":1101617,"title":"","content":"As they are both Urban tribes, there is a lot of movement between the Glasswalkers and Bone Gnawers. A Bone Gnawer cub with a knack for electronics may decide to Follow Cockroach and a Glasswalker cub who has trouble accepting authority may decided to join the Tribe of the streets. These interconnects keep relations between the two tribes amiable. <br /> <br /> I run Rite of Passage differently. Instead of a cub partitioning a particular totem, the Den Parent summons all the totems of the Garou Nation. The Sept Alpha sends the cub on a task needed by the Sept and appropriate to the cub's auspice. The Totems observe the cub completing the task. When the cub returns to the Caern, the tribal totems who will accept the cub are waiting. Sometimes the totem the cub wants to join is not present. The Cub then chooses which tribe they will join. <br /> <br /> Unicorn, Rat, and Cockroach are picker than most Garou think. Unicorn will not accept an closed minded Garou. Rat will not accept a proud and materialist cub and Cockroach despises stupidity. However, at least one of these totems will accept a cub. <br /> <br /> Get of Fenrir is a sexist tribe, but they don't condone rape. Stories of Garou fighting over kinfolk women are true, but arrangements are made before the challenge occurs. The Garou who wishes to mate with the kinfolk approaches a male Garou relative of the kinfolk. He challenges the relative for the right to mate with the kinfolk. The relative will talk to the kinfolk to make sure the Garou is acceptable to the kin. Then the two garou fight. If the challenging Garou does not put up a good fight, then the relative will tell him to come back when he is worthy of his sister/cousin/etc. If the challenger wins, then he is now mated. If a female kinfolk does not have any living relatives, she is in a bad situation. She can only hope the Sept Alpha will stand for her and protect her from Garou not of her choosing. Now the Fenrir have female Garou among their numbers, the tribe hasn't solidified the traditions for them. Some septs have the male kinfolk fight a male kinfolk relative for the right to mate with the Female Garou. Others have the male Kinfolk fight the Garou he wishes to make with to prove himself to her.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-08T15:12:44-07:00","id":1101753,"title":"","content":"I generally have challenges using mundane weapons (rather than natural weapons or magical weapons) or occurring in breed form unless it is to death. Death challenges only occur when Garou kill Kinfolk or when Garou are accused of given assistance to the Wyrm. Kinfolk may challenge Garou over points of honor and obtain Renown based off the difficulty of the challenge (an unarmed Kinfolk against unarmed Garou in breed form produces less than Renown than an unarmed Kinfolk against an armed Garou in Crinos form).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-08T16:45:12-07:00","id":1101788,"title":"","content":"There are no Black Furies. Instead there is an all-male tribe called the White Stallions. <br /> <br /> OK, not really. <br /> <br /> PENTEX is a much quieter and subtle entity, and it's Board of Directors is only seven people, who indirectly represent the Seven Deadly Sins. One is Samuel Haight, the disgruntled Kinfolk turned werewolf killer, who is not a pseudo-garou or anything else. He is, however, an action movie level badass (imagine Arnold Schwarzenegger in Predator with the mind of Alan Rickman in Die Hard) and does have magic that lets him take on a Crinos form. He represents Envy. Wrath is a rogue Silver Fang kinfolk broodmare who murdered her family and turned their wealth to destroying the Garou. Sloth is the great-grandson of the Pentex holding company's original founder, who just doesn't care about all the moral quagmires. <br /> <br /> Each facet of the Triat has it's fallen tribe. The Black Spiral Dancers, the Ivory Claws, and the Proteans (who no longer have any sort of fixed shape). <br /> <br /> And when I'm running Werewolf: The Dark Ages, the abuses of the Silver Crown occurred in the early 12th century, and now European Garou society is in a three-way civil war between the followers of the Falcon Banner, the Army of Thunder, and the Unicorn Crusade over who will be the new leaders of the Garou Nation. <br /> <br /> The shifters of North America used to have their own equivalent to the Ahadi or the Beast Courts. But that mostly fell apart during the North American War of Rage, though a number of folks fight the uphill struggle to reform it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-10T07:38:05-07:00","id":1102262,"title":"","content":"I usually tone Pentex waay down / make it less powerful, if I use it as a major antagonist at all. It is a little bit too &quot;Captain Planet Villain&quot; as written for my tastes.<br /> <br /> The impression I get from the official writing is that the taboos &amp; traditions of the Garou Nation are bad/outdated. I usually apply Chesterton's fence to this, and if PCs attempt to transgress a taboo without figuring out <i>why</i> it came about in the first place, I have it blow up in their faces. Not just because it makes stodgy irrational traditionalists angry, but because the taboo keeps some aspect of the Wyrm at bay or breaking it otherwise has negative unintended (by the PCs, but foreseen long ago by elders) consequences.<br /> <br /> The Ananasi were not quite as successful in the Insect Wars as they would like to believe. Not that the insect fera are a going concern, but there may be one or two frozen in amber somewhere around the world.<br /> <br /> I allow players to spend Gauntlet rating minus Rank Gnosis (minimum 1) points to step sideways (as long as they have a reflective surface). Doing so takes about 30 seconds, or the equivalent of two successes on a Gnosis roll.<br /> <br /> I'm a pretty flexible about what spirits teach what gifts, as long as it remains thematically appropriate.<br /> <br /> The Swords of Heimdall are kind of cringy Brow Scare stereotypes, so I run them not unlike how CTPhipps above does. They are still concerned about the fate of Nordic/German, and by some extension other European peoples, but no more than an average Uktena or Wendigo is concerned about Native Americans.<br /> <br /> Somewhat related to the above, of the Old World Garou, the Get of Fenris and the Silent Striders are the only tribes that actively worship the same gods/spirits as their typical Kinfolk human populations. Most tribes prefer to follow the more platonic Incarna. For example, Irish Garou might revere Horse, but consider Epona to be at best a flawed human interpretation of Horse.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://paizo.com/campaigns/RageAcrossIreland/gameplay\" target=\"_blank\">My W20 Play-by-Post Game</a>","edited":{"userid":2760,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2760-formosus","user":"Formosus","date":". 06-10-2017, 10:46 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2760-formosus","name":"Formosus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2760_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-10T10:44:59-07:00","id":1102297,"title":"","content":"<b>Pentex</b><br /> <br /> * One thing I do to differentiate Pentex from Captain Planet villains is the fact that Pentex is scary competent and amazingly effective at its job while also being something incredibly self-centered as well as short-sighted. About 1% of Pentex's executives are corrupted by the Wyrm and maybe 5% total believing in the supernatural period but they are capable of manipulating entire nations as well as making massive constructions happen over night. In our New York game, they had the US government put their PMC and Magadon drugs as part of the relief effort. They fix elections and start wars while waking up the profits.<br /> <br /> And....yet, still, a large portion of the executives KNOW they're going to destroy the world and selling out humanity.<br /> <br /> They just assume it isn't their problem, they'll be dead when it happens, or who cares about THEN when NOW is the issue. Garou, vampires, and even the Technocracy keep asusming there's some kind of deep hidden meaning to Pentex. But no, it's really it's a juggernaut based on short term gains and immense greed with all the metaphysical oomph of a rampaging rhino.<br /> <br /> * Pentex's ludicrous success is because it's actually the Eater of Souls. Specifically, it is the remnant Bane which survived the Croaton's sacrifice and eventually devoured the Weaver spirit of Merchantalism to become Capitalism. There's a much smaller pair of Glass Walker spirits in Trade and Prosperity not corrupted by it but they are in hiding. Capitalism notably devoured and killed the Weaver spirit of Communism with Pentex's help.<br /> <br /> It eventually plans to kill the Weaver and absorb it, which goes to show how all consuming its hunger is and it is powerful enough to might become the new Eater of Souls in the Umbra....if it hasn't always. To destroy this spirit would cause Pentex's supernatural gifts to all collapse and the company to spiral into dozens of simultaneous bankrupticies.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 06-10-2017, 02:52 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-10T11:39:22-07:00","id":1102315,"title":"","content":"For Pentex for myself I was influenced by 2 big things that found its way into my game:<br /> <br /> Wolfram and Heart: I figured here a lot of the evil in Pentex is them being a very successful company, run sure by some wyrm minions like Francisco but also in part by a lot of the employees making tainted pacts to ensure personal fortune and success. In this way some of their unsavory products or traditions occur to keep those patrons happy, but the employees themselves aren't screaming &quot;DAMN I'M EVIL&quot;. I think more along the line of Lindsey McDonald, they just want the good life, and the evil done to keep their patrons happy are not their problem. These high tear wyrm influences are just other customers to keep happy. I hope I explain it right, but its similar to the sentiment that Pentex was too Captain Planet, but at the same time I did like the idea of a supernatural evil company. <br /> <br /> Tim Burton's Batman: I thought the idea of products that create Fomori was a little weird, so I and would reduce your customer base too quickly. I also thought it could be too easily figured out and traced. So instead I took the idea that there was an &quot;unknown&quot; combination of products that would result in Fomor kinda like how Joker was killing people with his assorted &quot;Smylex&quot; in Tim Burton's Batman. <br /> <br /> On another note, years ago I found this odd d6 version of WtA. Not sure if it was official or anything but it was a soft cover physical book. It didn't have gifts but each of the tribes had an advantage to them. I thought the advantages were kinda neat (though most of them were lvl 1 gifts, and not all were equal), and my players liked them too so we kept those.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1179-celtspz","name":"CeltSPZ","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1179_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"835"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-10T12:12:58-07:00","id":1102326,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CeltSPZ</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1101014-w-ta-the-house-canon-thread-what-s-true-at-your-table?p=1102315#post1102315\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On another note, years ago I found this odd d6 version of WtA. Not sure if it was official or anything but it was a soft cover physical book. It didn't have gifts but each of the tribes had an advantage to them. I thought the advantages were kinda neat (though most of them were lvl 1 gifts, and not all were equal), and my players liked them too so we kept those.</div> </div> </div> </div>Care to elaborate on what sort of advantages they had? Also wondering if this was a GURPS book?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-10T12:27:56-07:00","id":1102330,"title":"","content":"I don't think it was a GURPS book, I remember it had a lot of known WtA art in it (like Ron Spencers) and could have sworn the copy looked like the revised book......not the GURP I always think of...but I could be wrong. A lot of them were basically lvl 1 gifts so I'll just list them off (even then its a bonus gift which is neat). My players have fun with it, so I keep it:<br /> <br /> Bone Gnawers: Blissful Ignorance<br /> Black Furies: Heightened Senses<br /> Children of Gaia: Mother's Touch<br /> Fianna: Resist Toxin<br /> Fenrir: Razor Claws<br /> Glass Walkers: Control Simple Machine<br /> Red Talons: Beast Speech<br /> Shadow Lords: Damage inflicted by them are at a +1 diff to soak<br /> Silent Striders: They redo a scene once per game, and it is explained away as having some sort of vison. I.e. a party member (or the player itself) dies and you restart the scene from the top, but you are stuck with the restart (no one ever plays Striders in my games for some odd reason despite this ability. They'll ask for Strider NPC's but never actually play one. As I said, not all of these are balanced but again, if my players are having fun....)<br /> Silver Fangs: -1 diff to all sword/klaive based melee rolls<br /> Star Gazers: Falling Touch<br /> Uktena: Sense Magic<br /> Wendigo: Call the Breeze and -1 diff to soak in the winter/cold climate (similar to their tribal flaw)<br /> <br /> Note: I tend to allow Fera in my games because I do like the changing breeds...and I feel guilty telling players &quot;no&quot; when it comes to character types. To bribe my players into playing Garou I tend to use these tribal advantages and not lean so much onto the tribal flaws.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1179,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1179-celtspz","user":"CeltSPZ","date":". 06-10-2017, 04:17 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1179-celtspz","name":"CeltSPZ","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1179_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"835"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-10T14:28:30-07:00","id":1102357,"title":"","content":"That sounds like one of those free demo versions that used to get made from time to time, maybe?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-10T14:33:43-07:00","id":1102359,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1101014-w-ta-the-house-canon-thread-what-s-true-at-your-table?p=1102297#post1102297\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">* One thing I do to differentiate Pentex from Captain Planet villains</div> </div> </div> </div>You know, in a lot of ways, I think Captain Planet was one of the worst things to ever happen to environmentalism, as it tried to teach a generation of kids that pollution happens because evil people just enjoy doing it for shits and giggles. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-10T14:36:23-07:00","id":1102361,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1101014-w-ta-the-house-canon-thread-what-s-true-at-your-table?p=1102359#post1102359\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You know, in a lot of ways, I think Captain Planet was one of the worst things to ever happen to environmentalism, as it tried to teach a generation of kids that pollution happens because evil people just enjoy doing it for shits and giggles.</div> </div> </div> </div>The reason for that is actually pretty sad. The villains were so cartoony, because the writers didn't want kids whose parents worked in factories and such to feel afraid or bad about their parents. So they made these villains cartoony. When they shouldn't have sidelined the questions and instead embraced the moral grayness.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-10T15:21:21-07:00","id":1102379,"title":"","content":"Kinfolk: As I've noted before in a few places, my Kinfolk sometimes come in a Kinfolk+ version. The Wolf-Blooded are prone to physical mutations which can lead to enhanced physical abilities, heightened senses, and increased predatory instincts. (In counterpart, there are Ape-Blooded wolf kin who have heightened reasoning ability, situational awareness and deviousness.) The Moon-Touched are prone to spiritual influences which can lead to shamanic talents, psychic abilities and insanity.<br /> <br /> Bastet: The Cealican are still alive and kicking, just because I kind of like them as a modern day Puss in Boots meets James Bond type thing.<br /> <br /> Gurahl: They have their own Auspices based on the seasons; Spring (Healers), Summer (Defenders), Autumn (Teachers), Winter (Priests), and lodges that don't depend on what type of bear they are or (for the most part) were they live, such as the Lodge of the Sky Mother (astronomers and prophets), Lodge of the Sleeping King (protectors of slumbering ancient Gurahl), and Lodge of the Cave Bear (all-ursine primitives who keep contact with the Red Talons). Also, the Okuma still exist as part of the Beast Courts, just because I like their role in Japanese and Korean folklore. And the Indian Gurahl are referred to as Jambavan. And there may or may not be Nandi in Africa. (It's never come up.)<br /> <br /> Rokea: They have long established human kinfolk lines in a handful of places, most notably Japan and various Polynesian cultures.<br /> <br /> Ratkin: I don't really use any of the existing plagues, or much of the Freak aspects. Instead, their little hordes are Tunnel/Sewer Rats (urban &quot;standard&quot; types), Swamp Rats (redneck hillbilly Deliverance types), Sea/River Rats (pirates and smugglers), Desert Rats (doomsday survivalists), Lab Rats (mad scientists and hackers), Plague Rats (disease cultists), and Pack Rats (collectors and thieves). And the Nezumi/Yao Shu as part of the Beast Courts include almost all of the above.<br /> <br /> Mokole: Only have five auspices, based on the castes from Exalted, just to simplify things.<br /> <br /> Nuwisha: Have no auspices or anything still, but do have Roads they follow, based on various &quot;tricky&quot; or &quot;wise&quot; animals. Those on the Raccoon Road are compulsive thieves, while followers of the Weasel Road are notorious for their violence and bloodlust, and ones on the Rattlesnake Road are delvers into often dangerous spiritual matters. There's maybe a dozen others. And one may jump from one road to another when they feel it's time to change.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-10T16:34:22-07:00","id":1102393,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1101014-w-ta-the-house-canon-thread-what-s-true-at-your-table?p=1102359#post1102359\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You know, in a lot of ways, I think Captain Planet was one of the worst things to ever happen to environmentalism, as it tried to teach a generation of kids that pollution happens because evil people just enjoy doing it for shits and giggles.</div> </div> </div> </div>Mind you, the problem actually becomes problematic when we have people like the POTUS who outright lie about the Paris Climate Change deal and global warming as well as a science data for minuscule gains in wealth. I also grew up in a part of the country where it was more profitable to lie about the amount of danger caused by chemical waste and pay for lawsuits than actually clean it up. That was in addition to constantly touting corporate loyalty before, well, let's just point out our local electrical company was owned by Enron.<br /> <br /> Real villains aren't Doctor Blight but they sure as hell resemble Hoggish Greedly.<br /> <br /> ...<br /> <br /> Yes, I watched the show. Linka was cute at my age then.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 06-10-2017, 07:41 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-10T18:10:53-07:00","id":1102406,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1101014-w-ta-the-house-canon-thread-what-s-true-at-your-table?p=1102357#post1102357\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That sounds like one of those free demo versions that used to get made from time to time, maybe?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Its possible, it was a friend of mine's book. I have never been able to find it again anywhere. It was odd, like the way Rage worked was you rolled your Rage at a diff 3 (again this was a d6), and each success equaled an extra action you could take, if you failed you got none, if you botched you lost your turn as you were too lost in Rage to act (paraphrasing there as its been years since I read it). It was...interesting...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1179-celtspz","name":"CeltSPZ","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1179_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"835"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-10T20:38:29-07:00","id":1102425,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1101014-w-ta-the-house-canon-thread-what-s-true-at-your-table?p=1102359#post1102359\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You know, in a lot of ways, I think Captain Planet was one of the worst things to ever happen to environmentalism, as it tried to teach a generation of kids that pollution happens because evil people just enjoy doing it for shits and giggles.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> *Looks at the Current Presidential administration*","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-10T22:35:11-07:00","id":1102435,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1101014-w-ta-the-house-canon-thread-what-s-true-at-your-table?p=1102425#post1102425\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> *Looks at the Current Presidential administration*</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, the unrealistic part of Pentex is that they had to have an agenda for world-domination versus the Wyrm just promising a bunch of people money.<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-11T16:45:23-07:00","id":1102648,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1101014-w-ta-the-house-canon-thread-what-s-true-at-your-table?p=1102435#post1102435\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah, the unrealistic part of Pentex is that they had to have an agenda for world-domination versus the Wyrm just promising a bunch of people money.<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Wyrm doesn't need to promise them shit. Having seen people who want to destroy the enviroment out of spite just to &quot;show it to the liberals&quot; the wyrm doesn't need to do shit. The wyrm can be completely passive.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-13T05:37:37-07:00","id":1103091,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1101014-w-ta-the-house-canon-thread-what-s-true-at-your-table?p=1102379#post1102379\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Gurahl: They have their own Auspices based on the seasons; Spring (Healers), Summer (Defenders), Autumn (Teachers), Winter (Priests), and lodges that don't depend on what type of bear they are or (for the most part) were they live, such as the Lodge of the Sky Mother (astronomers and prophets), Lodge of the Sleeping King (protectors of slumbering ancient Gurahl), and Lodge of the Cave Bear (all-ursine primitives who keep contact with the Red Talons). Also, the Okuma still exist as part of the Beast Courts, just because I like their role in Japanese and Korean folklore. And the Indian Gurahl are referred to as Jambavan. And there may or may not be Nandi in Africa. (It's never come up.)</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I really like this alternate interpretation of the Gurahl. I'd seriously consider adding this to my next game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Lead Writer for the Savage Age of Werewolf: the Apocalypse: <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/428750/Ghost-Lineages-The-Advanced-Players-Guide-to-the-Savage-Age\" target=\"_blank\">Ghost Lineages</a>, <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/312700/The-Rise-of-the-Garou-The-Savage-Age-Volume-Two\" target=\"_blank\">Rise of the Garou</a>, <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/331302/Tools-of-Extinction-The-Savage-Age-Volume-Three\" target=\"_blank\">Tools of Extinction</a>, <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/352717/Tribebook-Wlewa\" target=\"_blank\">Tribebook: Wlewa</a>.<br /> <br /> Want RPGs in libraries? Check out my book, <a href=\"http://www.abc-clio.com/ABC-CLIOCorporate/product.aspx?pc=A3951P\" target=\"_blank\">Dragons in the Stacks</a>. Now with <a href=\"http://www.ennie-awards.com/blog/2015-ennie-award-nominees-and-spotlight-winners/\" target=\"_blank\">awards</a>!<br /> \u200b","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1813-grimjaws","name":"grimjaws","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1813_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"134"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-13T05:38:41-07:00","id":1103092,"title":"","content":"Between the BSD (and other Fallen), the Fomori, and Pentex (and other corporations), the Wyrm does not really need to do anything.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-03T21:04:13-07:00","id":1137182,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1101014-w-ta-the-house-canon-thread-what-s-true-at-your-table?p=1103092#post1103092\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Between the BSD (and other Fallen), the Fomori, and Pentex (and other corporations), the Wyrm does not really need to do anything.</div> </div> </div> </div>To go further with this, the Wyrm doesn't need Pentex to actually be allied with it voluntarily and it's not, really. It just needs it to be itself.<br /> <br /> Pentex is Wrong Genre Savvy.<br /> <br /> Pentex is an awesome villain because it's actually not a bunch of Satanists worshiping Cthulhu but a group which really does think it's the Biggest Villains in the GameTM. The Pentex board of directors is under the impression it's the Technocracy, basically, and they're harnessing supernatural powers to make themselves super rich while also studying it to increase their power. They understand, intellectually, there's supernatural beings in other universes and gods and so on but they can't comprehend the idea they're not in CHARGE of these things on Earth.<br /> They may do the Satanic rite which kills 50 children via cancer by poisoning school lunches because they're appeasing a monster but mostly they're just spreading their power nad mind-control via television sets to gain power.<br /> <br /> The Wyrm understands the truth.<br /> <br /> They don't require Pentex to be anything more than what it is to &quot;win.&quot;<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-04T07:59:11-07:00","id":1137305,"title":"","content":"I generally keep most of the Garou Nation and Fera regressed back to their 2nd Edition identities (with some necessary exceptions with the Get of Fenris). I feel that 2nd edition presented Garou as overwhelmed by Rage (and with it- Bigotry, and Prejudice)- frustratingly incapable of getting their act together to stop the impending Apocalypse and it painted much of the state of the world as their own fault. They were murdering each other over pride and tribalism while the world was slipping further and further into decay. They took all the weaknesses and wickedness of humanity, mixed it with the jet fuel of inhuman Rage, and became the greatest representations of what they stood against... poisoned by their overwhelming shift toward homid-borns.<br /> <br /> The more modern versions of the Tribes presented in Revised and W20 make the Wars of Rage and the Impergium too hard to swallow for me, and make for a sizable theme-shift where &quot;Getting over themselves&quot; is no longer the primary impassable barrier to a Gaian victory. I grew up with a WtA where the theme was &quot;Defeat is inevitable, but we'll fight to the end and go down swinging&quot; and I like to preserve that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my mediocre WoD/Aeon/Exalted art at <a href=\"http://blackspinel.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://blackspinel.deviantart.com</a> ! It'll make you go &quot;Yup! That's pretty mediocre!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12162-crusher-of-cities","name":"Crusher-of-Cities","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12162_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"70"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-05T12:05:01-07:00","id":1137779,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crusher-of-Cities</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1101014-w-ta-the-house-canon-thread-what-s-true-at-your-table?p=1137305#post1137305\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The more modern versions of the Tribes presented in Revised and W20 make the Wars of Rage and the Impergium too hard to swallow for me, and make for a sizable theme-shift where &quot;Getting over themselves&quot; is no longer the primary impassable barrier to a Gaian victory. I grew up with a WtA where the theme was &quot;Defeat is inevitable, but we'll fight to the end and go down swinging&quot; and I like to preserve that.</div> </div> </div> </div>For the theme, that was the story to me by multiple media since I was a teen. The world is effed up, there is no true hope. Any victory you have will be nullified. Great then, not as much these days. It is all good to say that defeat is inevitable, but that then becomes a self-fulfilling prophesy. If there is no true will for change, change won't happen. To me, clawing a way to victory, a hard and painful road, is more fitting. Because hope doesn't mean there isn't darkness.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-05T12:30:06-07:00","id":1137788,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1101014-w-ta-the-house-canon-thread-what-s-true-at-your-table?p=1137779#post1137779\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> For the theme, that was the story to me by multiple media since I was a teen. The world is effed up, there is no true hope. Any victory you have will be nullified. Great then, not as much these days. It is all good to say that defeat is inevitable, but that then becomes a self-fulfilling prophesy. If there is no true will for change, change won't happen. To me, clawing a way to victory, a hard and painful road, is more fitting. Because hope doesn't mean there isn't darkness.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's a game set in a Gothic Punk universe. Punk is essentially noir in the fact the point is not to win because the world is never going to get better, the point is to FIGHT.<br /> <br /> You can run your game however you want but for me, 2nd Edition had more value storytelling wise as it often tackled difficult questions like race, prejudice, and institutional flaws.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-05T12:59:11-07:00","id":1137803,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1101014-w-ta-the-house-canon-thread-what-s-true-at-your-table?p=1137788#post1137788\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's a game set in a Gothic Punk universe. Punk is essentially noir in the fact the point is not to win because the world is never going to get better, the point is to FIGHT.<br /> <br /> You can run your game however you want but for me, 2nd Edition had more value storytelling wise as it often tackled difficult questions like race, prejudice, and institutional flaws.</div> </div> </div> </div>Punk is also the rage of the youth, and well, the rage has changed form. This is one of the reasons why I think Bone Gnawers as a tribe would change a lot, because the broke college graduate who cannot afford healthcare and has to scrape by is going to be the new majority. Given GWs represent the corporations and such, rejection and taking of rat as a symbol might happen.<br /> <br /> I think revisited still dealt with a lot of that stuff, it just wasn't as in your face as before. Hilariously enough, I think Children of Gaia revised basically was an unintentional study in ennui among those trying to help and why that is bad. On the positive side, Striders discussed things like abortion and post 9/11s effects to the tribe, wendigo is basically 80% Native american rage and so on.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-06T00:21:47-07:00","id":1137935,"title":"","content":"I have finished two months ago long run campaign around chasing the mythical fetishes each from the first pack members. Through their journey they were part of major changes in Black Fury tribe (at the end os session european part divided between younger and older members and soon it would erupt to open war - power struggle ruling circles), they were part of war in Chicago in under blood red moon, where the war was very different from original and barely escaped from the Abyss at the end sacrificing the life of alpha. <br /> <br /> Only to return to their home caern to face my new ideas, I'm going to make Skin Walkers major bad player with Haight as their leader - it would be something like kult not the tribe, puting BSD in the shadows. I'll try to make Wyrm more subtle. After the war in Chicago my players treat leeches like cattles for butchery. Time to change that and show them how manipulative and deadly Vampires can be.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1784-werewolf43","name":"werewolf43","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1784_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"315"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-13T20:32:40-07:00","id":1140073,"title":"","content":"I've made so many changes that I'll need to break this up into multiple posts. My setting is very compatible with the corebooks, but diverge to varying degrees on the supplemental material.<br /> <br /> <b>NPCs</b><br /> I really don't use the published NPCs and certainly not the ones related to the metaplot. However, when needed I like to name drop established characters simply to make it easier.<br /> <br /> <b>GAROU</b><br /> Glabro usually looks like Lon Chaney Wolfman or similar. If you want to look close to human, you need the Fair Glabro merit.<br /> <br /> Pure Breed 5 is no longer capable of being retained normally by Garou except through inbreeding. Pure Breed 5 families have only bred among themselves for over a century now. Pure Breed 4 is just beginning to become lost in the sense that most of those lineages are now beginning to produce Pure Breed 3 instead. Some of those families are now turning to inbreeding as well to \u201cpreserve\u201d the Breed. Outside of the Silver Fangs, Pure Breed 5 is almost non-existent and Pure Breed 4 is extremely rare. If you are a PB5 PC, you either one of the last of your kind or your family has some serious issues.<br /> <br /> I like to include things that align the game closer to actual werewolf legend and myth. Some of that I detailed <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/314196-werewolf-and-original-sources-folklore\">here</a>.<br /> <br /> <b>GAROU NATION</b><br /> There is much more infighting between septs, especially monotribal ones. Because many First Changers are essentially kidnapped by whichever tribe finds them first, poaching between tribes is a serious problem.<br /> <br /> Lunatics are a major problem in the setting. The combination of changes in human society, the breakdown of kinfolk communities, and toxins in the environment have greatly increased the number of Garou who never have their first change.<br /> <br /> Ronin are also a serious problem for the Garou. There are very large number of Ronin, definitely more than some of the smaller tribes. And while some Ronin are individual Garou living lives of exile, or trying to survive by going from sept to sept, most live their lives more in accordance to that of popular media of how werewolves exist. There are also several large societies or organizations of Ronin who have either bonded for survival or to try to \u201ccure\u201d themselves in various ways. In fact \u201cRonin\u201d is best used to describe a particular kind of these tribeless and outcast werewolves, the individuals described in the books. For the masses Vargr or Outlaw, is the better term.<br /> <br /> The Skin Dancers are a very, very old thing. Sam Haight, even if I decide he existed, was not the first one although he may have started the modern revival. Various occult tomes and kinfolk folklore exist describing how to do it. It is a know, but taboo subject among the kinfolk that there is a way for them to become a Garou, but the specifics aren't known.<br /> <br /> Man eating is a major problem within the nation as a whole with some tribes having major factions secretly devoted to it (all the tribal camps mentioned over the years). It has the same problem among the tribes that drug addiction has in human communities overall. Perhaps over five percent are habitual man eaters (meaning several times a year) with at least that amount of Garou who have done it at least once in their lives. This seemed to be the standard situation in 2nd edition if you read between the lines, but this was heavily ignored in Revised.<br /> <br /> <b>TRIBES</b><br /> Bunyip have never been actual Garou, but ashamed of wiping them out the Garou postumously \u201cadopted\u201d them as one. They're marsupials!<br /> <br /> The Bone Gnawers are not the most populous tribe. The idea of homeless bum werewolves conflicts so much with how I see werewolves that I can't accept that. Furthermore, even the tribebooks mention that much of the tribe is comprised of the \u201cRabble\u201d who don't seem to be involved in the tribe at all. I simply took this part of the tribe and made it into Ronin. I've also made it a deep metaplot point in my own chronicles that there is something seriously wrong with Rat as the totem. Rat in fact is falling to the Wyrm, but in a process which may still take decades or even centuries. This is something some Bonegnawers suspect, but they are proceeding very cautiously.<br /> <br /> Children of Gaia are different because I portray Unicorn differently as explained in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/902383-heretical-thoughts-on-unicorn\">this thread</a>. They are less about \u201cpeace\u201d and more about protecting purity and innocence although they still serve as mediators.<br /> <br /> The major reason the Get of Fenris get so much blame for World War II and Nazism is that it is a smear job orchestrated by the other tribes. While the Get deserve some of the opprobrium heaped on them, it is no more and often less than the blame other tribes deserve for their disastrous handling of the Soviet Union which nevertheless doesn't seem to result in any permanent shame on them. The reason for the smear campaign is simple, there was a strong movement among the Get of Fenris in the thirties and forties to make a bid for leadership of the Garou Nation. They thought (incorrectly) that National Socialist Germany was going to forge a new, more Gaian order for humanity. The Nazis had a strong environmental movement and passed the first anti-pollution and endangered species laws on the planet. They wanted to return people back to the land. Some wanted to revive a pagan spirituality which the Get believed could become the basis for a more Gaian religion. Most important of all, they were enemies of that horrible Wyrm-ridden Soviet Union and would have wiped it out. The Swords of Heimdall weren't so much racists (although they were that too), but the camp of Get who wanted to make a bid for leadership of the Nation since the Silver Fangs were obviously failing and the Shadow Lords just could not be trusted. Of course the bid failed, but it panicked everyone that the tribe thought to be the mightiest would even attempt that so the Silver Fangs made sure it would never happen again by a very, very, very successful smear campaign. But the Swords of Heimdall survive, but find it very hard to recruit. (Heimdall was the god who created the social classes among men, and therefore established the warrior nobility).<br /> <br /> I've tried to make the Red Talons more complex and nuanced by building up the spirituality around Griffon as explained <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/912624-heretical-thoughts-on-griffin-and-the-red-talons\">here</a>. What homids call the Whelp's Compromise are Red Talons who go out among humanity so they can learn more about them and return home with more knowledge. Usually when they are done with their rumspringa, these Red Talons have an even lower opinion of humanity than they did afterwards. But some think there is hope.<br /> <br /> Silent Striders aren't really werewolves, but werejackals. Not so much a change as stating the obvious. But since they are still canis and can interbreed with wolves, they actually are Garou. Their high breed form looks like the Golden Jackal and African Golden Wolf (Canis lupaster - only recently classified as wolf, but previously though to be a subspecies of the Golden Jackal). Note that the African Golden Wolf is not a subspecies of the Grey Wolf. Canis lupaster are even more genetically distant from real wolves than coyotes are. This is less a change than a clarification.<br /> <br /> Silver Fangs only demonstrate madness as a result of vicious inbreeding to preserve high amounts of Pure Breed. There is no curse that accounts for it. It is a product that has only really shown up in the last two hundred years. Clan Crescent Moon is so dominant as a royal house and occupies so much land that it in turn is divided up into \u201cducal houses,\u201d which accounts for some political conflict within the clan and for different types of human ethnicities and pure breed appearances.<br /> <br /> Stargazers are not the \u201cAsian\u201d tribe. They are mystics and philosophers who seek desolate areas like mountain tops so they can philosophize and meditate in peace. There is certainly a concentration of Stargazers in Asia because it is home to some very tall mountain ranges around the culmen mundi, but they have long standing communities around the Alps, Pyrenees, and Caucasus in Europe, and the Alborz, Zagros, and Taurus mountains in the Middle East. Once the Americas opened up, the tribe was happy to go to the Rocky Mountains and in Alaska.<br /> <br /> There are many Garou tribes in Asia. The Boli Zouishe are the Glass Walkers. The Hakken are just as much as Shadow Lords as anyone in Europe. Shadow Lords also have kinfolk all along the steppe in Central Asia, Mongolia, and Manchuria. There are Silver Fangs of House Blood Red Crest in China although the tribe never succeeded in establishing themselves in China as they did among the feudal lords of Europe after the fall of Rome. In the north among the Siberian tribes are plenty of Silver Fangs who belong to Clan Crescent Moon. Bonegnawers are in China too. Red Talons as well. And the Children of Gaia. There is no reason to divide up the Garou or even the Fera into a human cultural arrangement.<br /> <br /> <br /> I'll get to some of the others later. When I get to the Wyrm, there's lots of changes from canon.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3046,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","user":"Black Fox","date":". 09-14-2017, 02:23 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-13T22:38:25-07:00","id":1140085,"title":"","content":"Blackfox if they ever did do a Werewolf storytellers vault I'd love to see an expansion on your COG and Red Talons stuff.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-14T04:59:25-07:00","id":1140131,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1101014-w-ta-the-house-canon-thread-what-s-true-at-your-table?p=1140073#post1140073\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Lunatics are a major problem in the setting. The combination of changes in human society, the breakdown of kinfolk communities, and toxins in the environment have greatly increased the number of Garou who never have their first change.<br /> <br /> Ronin are also a serious problem for the Garou. There are very large number of Ronin, definitely more than some of the smaller tribes. And while some Ronin are individual Garou living lives of exile, or trying to survive by going from sept to sept, most live their lives more in accordance to that of popular media of how werewolves exist. There are also several large societies or organizations of Ronin who have either bonded for survival or to try to \u201ccure\u201d themselves in various ways. In fact \u201cRonin\u201d is best used to describe a particular kind of these tribeless and outcast werewolves, the individuals described in the books. For the masses Vargr or Outlaw, is the better term.</div> </div> </div> </div>I've actually written a similar group, the Currs: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/916359-a-npc-antagonist-template-for-people-to-use?p=917432#post917432\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...432#post917432</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-14T15:32:39-07:00","id":1140341,"title":"","content":"I think Lunatics and Ronin are a much underutilized tool in the setting. They are an excellent way to introduce a more traditional or &quot;cinematic&quot; werewolf into the setting that is not disruptive. Your group the Currs is a good example of what could be done with them. <br /> <br /> Ronins make good foils for Garou especially those not exiled Garou for crimes, but who have adapted to the Change entirely outside Garou culture. Simply by refusing to join the Garou Nation, they are rebuking and insulting them. But as antagonists they are not obviously of the Wyrm, and therefore produce a different dynamic of how to deal with them. Since Ronins are almost universally going to be Homids, they only start with 1 Gnosis so their connection to Gaia is extremely weak and therefore there is no real loyalty to Gaia even if told about it. And while young kids who Change are young enough to become indoctrinated by Garou, Lost Cubs are much less likely to accept this new culture uncritically.<br /> <br /> The books' traditional Ronin, someone exiled for a crime who goes from sept to sept looking for scraps and occasionally working dirty jobs at them, has a role in the game too. But I can think of lots more things I can do with werewolves who aren't affiliated with the Garou Nation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-15T03:41:38-07:00","id":1140474,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1101014-w-ta-the-house-canon-thread-what-s-true-at-your-table?p=1140341#post1140341\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think Lunatics and Ronin are a much underutilized tool in the setting. They are an excellent way to introduce a more traditional or &quot;cinematic&quot; werewolf into the setting that is not disruptive. Your group the Currs is a good example of what could be done with them.<br /> <br /> Ronins make good foils for Garou especially those not exiled Garou for crimes, but who have adapted to the Change entirely outside Garou culture. Simply by refusing to join the Garou Nation, they are rebuking and insulting them. But as antagonists they are not obviously of the Wyrm, and therefore produce a different dynamic of how to deal with them. Since Ronins are almost universally going to be Homids, they only start with 1 Gnosis so their connection to Gaia is extremely weak and therefore there is no real loyalty to Gaia even if told about it. And while young kids who Change are young enough to become indoctrinated by Garou, Lost Cubs are much less likely to accept this new culture uncritically.<br /> <br /> The books' traditional Ronin, someone exiled for a crime who goes from sept to sept looking for scraps and occasionally working dirty jobs at them, has a role in the game too. But I can think of lots more things I can do with werewolves who aren't affiliated with the Garou Nation.</div> </div> </div> </div>Currs were born when I read so many critiques of the Garou Nation and thought &quot;Why doesn't the SETTING address these?&quot;. Hence, the Currs were born as my take on how some garou would take to the Nation.<br /> <br /> Even if it messes up with the 'garou are rare' detail, I do agree. I think having ronin serve as the result of not fitting in or just never being found is interesting. Especially once you look outside homids. Lupus ronin who try to still live as wolves, lupus ronin who go all Romasanta and start trying to use humans for their own goals. Or lupus ronin who join those seeking for a cure, wanting to return to their old state. Essentially taking a page out of Forsaken's book with Ghost Wolves XD<br /> <br /> This is also why I don't like the idea of the Bitten in MET, it screws with the idea that you are born garou and nothing you do will change it. Also why DNA never quite worked for me, it is an org studying werewolves from the outside. The want for a cure should come from the -inside-.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-15T13:29:14-07:00","id":1140621,"title":"","content":"Alright here are some more changes I do for my chronicles.<br /> <br /> FERA<br /> I go very low on the population of the Fera. In general, I try to tone down the population of supernatural creatures to keep things \u201crealistic\u201d and not \u201cgonzo\u201d so I'm very conservative compared to some STs. I rarely ever use them although if the geography of the setting indicates there may be some Fera there, I'll put one or a few in my chronicle notes.<br /> <br /> The vast majority of Bastet reflect the ethnicity of the regions the werecreatures inhabit. Ethnic European homid bastet are extremely rare unless there is good historical reason there is a population for them. The Ceilican are practically extinct and only exist because I like Val Lewton's 1942 movie Cat People. A few are born every generation, but they have no practical knowledge of their ancestry or Fera culture although there are resources out there that could help them. Since games are mainly set in North America, that means Pumonca and Qualmi could be present. I wouldn't use others unless there was a major plot/story that needed it.<br /> <br /> Corax have their own issues between their Eurasian and North American homid populations like the Garou, but they've handled it better.<br /> <br /> Kitsune exists outside of Japan although the tribe's population is better preserved in East Asia then elsewhere. There is a reason Europeans know the exploits of Reynard the Fox.<br /> <br /> Mokole are werecrocodiles and have no dinosaur form. They do have a form of Gaian memory and therefore knowledge of a past before the arrival of man, but my prehistory is very different than published ones as the Changing Breeds were only created about 12,000 years ago as the Ice Age ended and the Holocene began.<br /> <br /> Nuwisha are considered the little cousin or nephew of the Pure Ones. Therefore the Wendigo and Uktena have strong ties to them, and the rest of the Garou Nation is very accepting to them as much as they can tolerate Coyote. They are treated less like they are one of the Fera separate from the Garou and more like the red headed stepchild who is still family.<br /> <br /> Ratkin do not have a large population. Too many of those infected with the Birthing Plague just die. I like the idea they possibly pose a future threat, but not an incipient one.<br /> <br /> SPIRITS<br /> As per the old White Wolf errata, Scrags have only 6 Rage. This was something that really should have been updated in W20.<br /> <br /> I do my best to make spirits an important part of the game. Named spirits are important part of the chronicle's NPCs. I have my players document every spirit who teaches them Gifts. I try to have at least half a dozen or so Jagglings around the area I can use as the basis for spirit interactions between themselves, NPC Garou, and the PCs. Spirits have their likes and dislikes, and being friendly to one may mean some other spirit becomes not so friendly. I roleplay most of my Gaian spirits based on what I read in Aesop's Fables, Bambi, and Watership Down. It gives Theurges something to do, and even for the other auspices usually the Pack Totem can act as interpreter for them.<br /> <br /> Bat and Whipporwill were originally Gaian totems corrupted by the Wyrm. I've added several more cases of such spirits. They are either spirits of animals traditionally associated with witchcraft, or are vectors of diseases. If Garou see them, they become suspicious they are being spied on by the Wyrm. Such spirits include Toad, Moth, Tick, and Fly. Their Incarna serve the Wyrm now. In addition, there are spirits which are not fully corrupted, but many individual spirits serve the Wyrm even if their Incarna does not. They include Vulture, Mosquito, Spider, and Rat. Temperate and artic mosquitoes are geneally Gaian and allied to Wendigo; but tropical Mosquitoes that spread disease are in service to the Wyrm. Most Rat spirits are Gaian, but there are a noticeable number of Wyrm-aligned ones. (Obviously this is deeply embrassing for the Bone Gnawers). And Black Cats serve the Wyrm just because, the evil little bastards. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Mother Night is a major antagonist in the setting, a powerful spirit allied with the Wyrm. She, her brood, and her servants (including Fomori) are up there with Black Spiral Dancers and PENTEX as a Wyrm faction. Mother Night and her brood are not the night spirits who love Gaia. Mother Night is the primeval darkness that exsisted before Helios. She is the terrible darkness and the evil that would happen if not for the light of Luna. Mother Night is responsible for the most of the malevolent witch cults in history, and is responsible for all sorts of monsters that thrive in night. The vampires who call themselves Bahari worship her in one of her guises.<br /> <br /> I have lots of Wyrm sorcerers whose magic is mainly summoning various Banes to serve them. Most Banes printed in the books are actually not very appropriate for this so I have to make my own. (There are some like Scryers that can work as is fine, and home made spirit servants of some of the Black Spiral Dancer totems are also good). Many are based on either real folklore or the Call of Cthulhu roleplaying game. Umbral Stalkers (Dimensional Shamblers) and Malfean Steeds (Byakhee) can be very useful. Plus they make serviceable opponents for PCs should a fight break out.<br /> <br /> \u200bStill more to come.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-16T13:42:46-07:00","id":1140896,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1101014-w-ta-the-house-canon-thread-what-s-true-at-your-table?p=1140621#post1140621\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Alright here are some more changes I do for my chronicles.<br /> <br /> <br /> Mokole are werecrocodiles and have no dinosaur form. They do have a form of Gaian memory and therefore knowledge of a past before the arrival of man, but my prehistory is very different than published ones as the Changing Breeds were only created about 12,000 years ago as the Ice Age ended and the Holocene began.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>So does this mean we won't get to see a write up on Dragon? I really liked how you spun Rat (I'd thought similar thoughts, but in my game i have some big Ratkin and Bone Gnawer fans who'd be pissed if I followed through with it), Unicorn and Griffin. I was hoping to one day see how you'd spin Dragon and Turtle.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1179-celtspz","name":"CeltSPZ","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1179_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"835"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-16T22:47:02-07:00","id":1140989,"title":"","content":"Thanks for the kind words and interest. I'm very unlikely to ever do a write up for Dragon or Turtle. I originally worked on the other totems because there were things that affected my games. For Rat, there were things I immediately saw based on the actual material which seemed obvious to me, but which the writers of the materials didn't see themselves (I find it interesting you had similar thoughts). For Unicorn, it was to better align it with how Unicorn was depicted in legend and which I thought made the tribe better. For Griffin, it was to help provide more depth for the Red Talons which I thought was really needed. These were all things with direct relevance to my chronicles and possibly the PCs during character creation. I have never really used the Mokole in my chronicles so I just don't have the interest in how their totems affect them.<br /> <br /> I haven't posted anything on the other tribal totems because I'm fairly happy with how they are presented canonically. I don't have much to add. I do have some thoughts on Cockroach and Glass Walkers, but haven't come to a satisfactory result. I have a Word file with various ideas posted in it, but nothing has clicked that has brought them together. Maybe some day.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-17T13:18:33-07:00","id":1141182,"title":"","content":"After first reading about the Ratkin I had a hard time seeing them as forces of the wyld, so much as of the balance wyrm. I had an idea that they were going &quot;crazy&quot; not so much due to all the wyld energy exposure and the time in the Umbra so much as a result of the wyrm's fall from grace. I had a few players who were huge Ratkin and Gnawer fans though, and I dropped fleshed the idea out because they thought I was just picking on them. <br /> <br /> As for Unicorn and Griffin I really thought your spin helped redeem both tribes and flesh them out better. It veered away from blatant stereotypes and added new life to them. I actually started to adopt a lot of those write ups for my own games (figured you wouldn't mind, or why share it anyway). It also helped explain WHY some of the negative stereotypes did come about too, which was nice. You didn't reject the cannon you added to it (that's how I read it). <br /> <br /> Also I found it interesting that in Shattered Dreams they have a list of proto-tribes and among them were &quot;Luna's Chosen&quot; who later split into the Silver Fangs and Red Talons....showing a kin ship you wrote about. I wondered if the authors saw your post (I couldn't remember the time frame and if it came at the right time or if it was a odd coincidence).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1179-celtspz","name":"CeltSPZ","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1179_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"835"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-17T17:42:31-07:00","id":1141265,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CeltSPZ</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1101014-w-ta-the-house-canon-thread-what-s-true-at-your-table?p=1141182#post1141182\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">After first reading about the Ratkin I had a hard time seeing them as forces of the wyld, so much as of the balance wyrm.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Wyld is actually a hard concept to define so I usually think carefully before I say, &quot;That's not part of the Wyld&quot;. But I agree with you that very little of the Ratkin seemed to fit the Wyld concept. The fecundity of rats and their ability to flourish even in Man's cities do associate with that, but things like &quot;their purpose is to kill people so they don't overpopulate&quot; and &quot;they spread disease&quot; are definitely not Wyld concepts. In fact it was going over the Ratkin book which prompted me to rethink some of the things I'd read in the Bone Gnawer tribebook.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I had a few players who were huge Ratkin and Gnawer fans though, and I dropped fleshed the idea out because they thought I was just picking on them. </div> </div> </div>It can be difficult when the ST's conceptions clash with the PCs especially if the players think your ideas invalidate their own concepts. This is one reason I do not make this very obvious in my own chronicles that Rat is falling. I just show how some NPCs are acting because that is the case so the players can react against it and come up with their own ideas of why that is. There is no problem having heroic Bone Gnawer and Ratkin, and Rat hasn't fallen yet (and who knows, may not).<br /> <br /> Incidentally I once played in an online game and sent a PC concept in for sanctioning that was he was part of a small group of Bone Gnawers who were concerned about this and were starting to compile information to determine if their fears were valid. STs rejected it with comments like &quot;Your PC is insane and whatever NPC group he belongs to must be part of the Wyrm for it is impossible for anyone to come to that conclusion.&quot; My reply was &quot;OK, if that is your ruling. I will create another concept. But here are the reasons I think it is possible for someone to come to this conclusion.&quot; The response then was &quot;All those things you mentioned don't exist in this game. There is no Rabble. There are no strong ties to Nosferatu vampires. No rumors that vampires are part of the Ring of Shadows which leads the tribe. The tribe is just as strong as obeying the Litany as the others, it is just a different interpretation...&quot; and so on. I just asked myself who is really the one departing from canon here?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> As for Unicorn and Griffin I really thought your spin helped redeem both tribes and flesh them out better. It veered away from blatant stereotypes and added new life to them. I actually started to adopt a lot of those write ups for my own games (figured you wouldn't mind, or why share it anyway). It also helped explain WHY some of the negative stereotypes did come about too, which was nice. You didn't reject the cannon you added to it (that's how I read it). </div> </div> </div>My one commandment is to not invalidate anything in the original corebooks (a bit harder with W20 because it includes so much from other material). The corebook should be the one thing everyone agrees on. But I consider anything in the supplements as things an ST can use or ignore as he sees fit. Many people seemed to have trouble with Children of Gaia as a tribe, and didn't know what to do with Red Talons as anything other than villains who would blow up the setting. So I shared it in the hopes it would help others with their own games.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Also I found it interesting that in Shattered Dreams they have a list of proto-tribes and among them were &quot;Luna's Chosen&quot; who later split into the Silver Fangs and Red Talons....showing a kin ship you wrote about. I wondered if the authors saw your post (I couldn't remember the time frame and if it came at the right time or if it was a odd coincidence). </div> </div> </div>I haven't read Shattered Dreams so it is neat to learn it has something that mirrors one of my own ideas. However, I think it was written (and perhaps even published) before I posted anything on the tribal totems. It just goes to show a lot of one's own ideas occur to others as well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3046,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","user":"Black Fox","date":". 09-17-2017, 08:45 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-19T12:52:28-07:00","id":1141856,"title":"","content":"PENTEX<br /> Many changes here as I find the canonical version cartoonish and ridiculous. There is a core PENTEX, but many of the PENTEX subsidiaries are actually unrelated companies somehow involved with the Wyrm. Others are inadvertently spreading Wyrm taint somehow, but aren't part of any occult conspiracy. Some of the companies I can't see in anyway as having real value to the game (as part of some Wyrm cult) in which case I use them merely as names for companies in the setting as needed.<br /> <br /> PENTEX still exists based on a core of companies responsible for most of the major industrial pollutants on the planet so they are mainly heavy industry and chemicals plus other manufacturing that may produce particularly toxic waste. They are much less likely to sell branded products to consumers as they are to sell raw materials to the companies that do. PENTEX itself is a holding company, but mainly a conspiracy that extends beyond it. Deep Umbral spirits of the Wyrm seek to anti-terraform Earth into an entirely new ecosystem so that those \u201cspirits\u201d can arrive and make this planet their new home. They've recruited greedy, short sighted humans to assist them in this, some of whom become Toad fomori. They only create other Fomori in an attempt to defend themselves from werewolves. This PENTEX is heavily inspired by the movie They Live, and yes the look of the aliens there is how the Toad fomori appear. And the billboards say things like CONSUME and OBEY once you peek into the Umbra in those areas that are dominated by the Wyrm and Weaver (areas where there are Blights and also CyberRealm and Scar). John Nada would simply be a normal human who achieved partial enlightenment so that he could contact the Periphery. As such, I don't use any of the \u201cBoard of Directors\u201d ever mentioned in any of the books. Just for convenience, I might reuse some of the names. But I don't use anything like there's a Malkavian anti-tribu or Black Spiral Dancer on the board.<br /> <br /> Endron Oil is allied with the PENTEX conspiracy, but has another agenda. It is in the service of a particular Bane (once imprisoned by the Uktena) it freed during initial oil drilling over a century ago. That Bane controls the company through its own cult, and the companies' drilling operations are to free similar Banes. Despite the similarity of names, Endron is not based on Enron, but is a much more traditional oil company. I keep a lot of the original backstory of Premium Oil and the Lassiter family for this.<br /> <br /> Magadon Pharmaceutical is its own separate Wyrm conspiracy controlled by cults devoted to Wakshaa and Hrugg. The cult wants to produce a new breed of man so it can survive the Apocalypse. They produce some very awful Fomori. PENTEX and they are aware of each other, and occasionally cooperate but since they serve different masters they don't get along and have different goals.<br /> <br /> Black Dog Game Factory exists as its own separate thing, and they are just your traditional Wyrm occultists who hope to recruit new people into \u201cSatanic\u201d worship through occult inspired RPGs. It has no ties to PENTEX and the Banes involved are very different. I just liked the idea of an actual RPG occult conspiracy. However, I've never come up with any major plots about it. Just little ones like the friend of a young kinfolk to a PC getting messed up in it so I can use their backstory for minor plots.<br /> <br /> Companies like King Breweries and O'Tolley's do produce Wyrm tainted products consumed by people, but their occult involvement is inadvertent. All they really do is produce enough low grade crap that it \u201cclogs\u201d people's system enough to cut them off from Gaia on an instinctual level. It also desensitizes people enough to open them up to future Bane possession once exposed to actual toxic stuff. Key members of these companies do belong to a Wyrm cult controlled by PENTEX who make sure their products are tainted, but that is really their only role. Nobody becomes a Fomori because they ate a quarter pounder with cheese.<br /> <br /> But many of the other named companies are not simply involved in any Wyrm conspiracy. They are placeholder names that I use either as background, or perhaps as some plot if I need a company like them. But the plot likely has nothing to do with PENTEX, but maybe it might involve vampires or one of my other Wyrm cults. And if it does, the amount of actual control or influence they have may be far less than absolute. More often than not, they are just ordinary companies who if they do something anti-Gaian, it is because they are greedy and shortsighted, not members of a Wyrm cult.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-10T12:46:20-08:00","id":1157616,"title":"","content":"We had major revisions for the tribes.<br /> <br /> To begin, the Black Furries aren't the Wyld tribe. That is now the Red Talons shtick. It feels more appropriate and gives the Talons a little bit more of an ideology than just being the Lupus tribe.<br /> <br /> The Bone Gnawers and Glass Walkers have been merged. It's more the Gnawers, left alone in the cities, evolved into embracing urban and technological spirits, turning into a tribe similar to the Glass Walkers. It gives the hybrid tribe more fluidity than either being city elite or bums, but ranges across the spectrum of urban society. Plus I like the Glass Walkers having a more Bone Gnawer-esque social structure and ideological influence about what they do.<br /> <br /> Another tribal merger are the Children of Gaia and Stargazers into the Children of Derga. This hybrid tribe I feel compliments each together than existing separately. Their homeland is in India and Tibet, and then they spread out from there. Stargazers could exist as a faction of the Children that left to fully join the Beast Courts.<br /> <br /> Shadow Lords are all Hakken, and are more spread out across East Asia than being solely in Japan. There's enough European tribes, and the Euro Shadow Lords often come off as one dimensional 'evil Silver Fangs' that have this almost cartoonish eternal aim to over throw the Silver Fangs, but fail to do so (though in revised I understand this has been given a better history, but still). As Hakken, and having kin among the East Asian civilizations, as well as being members of the Beast Courts, gives them more of a natural opposition to the Silver Fangs.<br /> <br /> Silver Fangs, instead of being associated with a European state that didn't come into existence until the middle of the Medieval era have replaced the Shadow Lords as the tribe whose human kin ran with the steppe peoples of Asia. They used the various steppe empires to dominate, and it wasn't until the Mongol Empire that they really put effort in breeding with the various nobilities of Europe and Asia.<br /> <br /> Get of Fenris and Fianna are more spread out across the European and Mediterranean spectrum since Celtic and Germanic peoples got around since the Classic Age. Like for instance, you can find Get septs in North Africa thanks to the Vandal Empire.<br /> <br /> The Siberakh are a full tribe, and considered 'lost sibling' to the Pure Tribes. They have kin among the Inuit, and served as bridge between the Pure Tribes and the rest of the Garou. They also found themselves acting as mediators between the Silver Fangs and Shadow Lords over their rivalries across Asia.<br /> <br /> Kucha Ekundu are another sub-tribe that I've been thinking of elevating to full tribe.<br /> <br /> The White Howlers/Black Spiral Dancers have been changed from a Pict originating tribe to having their human kin among the Baltic and Uralic peoples. They fell in the middle ages during the Baltic genocides.<br /> <br /> No notable changes to the Silent Striders or Bunyip. Though for the latter, in regards to what they did with the Ajaba, I'm inclined to say they were changed by Gaia in the same way to be their own changing breed. Then there's also the option they simply bred with Dingos too, avoiding all the weirdness.<br /> <br /> More or less we wanted to have the Garou of the Eastern Hemisphere to be more Eurasian, with some overlap with the Beast Courts, and down play the more ethnic stereotypes that a lot of the tribes fall into. We also tried to emphasize the tribes being more allied camps that are linked by their totem affiliations.<br /> <br /> The umbra, particularly in the Americas was completely redone, but that would take a massive post to get into that. This goes into how we redid the entire supernatural world of the Americas to reflect more the legacy of indigenous institutions rather than the bland generic setting it turned out to be in cannon.<br /> <br /> As for the Wyrm we've largely ignored Pentex, and focused more on fighting BSDs, Banes, and echoing mythic cycles. It fits WtA better in our opinions. We've toyed around with replacements and reforms for Pentex here and there, but never settled on anything concrete.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":21481,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/21481-onkwe","user":"Onkwe","date":". 11-10-2017, 05:59 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/21481-onkwe","name":"Onkwe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar21481_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"162"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-10T13:03:20-08:00","id":1157621,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Onkwe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1101014-w-ta-the-house-canon-thread-what-s-true-at-your-table?p=1157616#post1157616\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> As for the Wyrm we've largely ignored Pentex, and focused more on fighting BSDs, Banes, and echoing mythic cycles. It fits WtA better in our opinions. We've toyed around with replacements and reforms for Pentex here and there, but never settled on anything concrete.</div> </div> </div> </div>Corporations just being corporations tends to lead to an effective enough set of dug-in antagonists that are coiled around life in the modern, industrialized world.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-10T13:10:45-08:00","id":1157623,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1101014-w-ta-the-house-canon-thread-what-s-true-at-your-table?p=1157621#post1157621\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Corporations just being corporations tends to lead to an effective enough set of dug-in antagonists that are coiled around life in the modern, industrialized world.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> That's our feeling as well. At best I see more interlinked Wyrm cults and BSD kinfolk (which go hand in hand) and their puppets worming their way throughout numerous corporations and other institutions than it all being concentrated into one megacorp.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/21481-onkwe","name":"Onkwe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar21481_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"162"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-10T13:50:07-08:00","id":1157629,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1101014-w-ta-the-house-canon-thread-what-s-true-at-your-table?p=1157621#post1157621\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Corporations just being corporations tends to lead to an effective enough set of dug-in antagonists that are coiled around life in the modern, industrialized world.</div> </div> </div> </div>Plus, it kinda shows that you don't need to be wyrmy at all yourself to end up selling tainted products. Given how brands travel around the world, just a regular coke machine in some backwater gas station in Lappland can be tainted due to assiosication.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-18T12:28:36-08:00","id":1168598,"title":"","content":"Since I run a crossover game between VtM, DtF, Mage(albeit they're background fluff mostly) and WtA, its mostly fluff material thats changed. For example God/The Creator is at the top followed by the Loyal Heavenly Host and the Fallen as the makers of everything with the Triat, Gaia and the God-Machine(imported from CoD) as part of the system left behind to maintain Creation. Pentex is still evil as they are in canon, but they're nowhere near as monolithic and has been pushed out of the military industry market in europe due to competitors being better(minus russia whom they're selling stuff to)(though they did succeed in some significant things elsewhere in a DtF and VtM crossover story) and due to WW3 being a metaplot ongoing event.<br /> <br /> Other than that I just decided that with everything going poorly, the Nagah has decided to slowly emerge from their long exile, but only on their terms(we're working on setting up a nagah and vtm crossover story that takes place deep behind the ww3 frontlines).<br /> <br /> Mechanics we use mostly in a lite fashion as we care more about roleplaying well and thus only use it for combat that doesn't involve weak goons as rolling for everything just slows down things way too much(and due to health reasons I have serious problems remembering mechanics even when having the pdfs open to help).<br /> <br /> About it really.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13674-amalasuintha","name":"Amalasuintha","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13674_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"123"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-20T03:45:26-08:00","id":1169043,"title":"","content":"I'm planning to run a ne WtA game soon and I want to try a few big changes.<br /> <br /> First is removing Stepping Sideways<br /> It might make the game too anchored to the mundane world but I'd like to remove the ability of Stepping Sideways and leave the ability to enter Umbra only where the Gauntlet is really thin, like in Caerns. Also penumbra and stepping sideways almost freely complicates things both for me and players a lot (at least that's how I feel when running the game). But I think I'd leave to Garou the ability to peek into the Penumbra, because it builds a lot of atmosphere. Let's call it Looking Sideways <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Second Garou are more rare with each passing year<br /> Due to hunts, extermination, Losing the Wolf, endagerment of the wolf species and other stuff, as per 2017 the Nation is basically no more (if ever existed) and the surviving Garou are let's say half of the supposed number from official setting, if not less. And half of the surviving went into hiding, almost given up the fight, some even trying to have normal lives with human jobs (ugh). But the good fight still must be fought. Will the characters stand up for the hopeless fight? Without anyone leading them? Taking charge? Ok I know, it won't happen. Players taking charge. Amusing.<br /> <br /> I think I'll keep the Looking Sideways instead of Stepping Sideways idea.<br /> And for the second idea I'll think I'll limit myself into removing a lot of politics. I'm looking for a more straightforward and visceral game. Politics can be fun but tend to distract from the &quot;primal&quot; premises, and I'd like to try for once to run a game that hits some emotional chords in an easy way","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Ever since the Followers of Set rebranded themselves as The Ministry, I can barely keep a straight face around them.&quot; - Ramona","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/15944-ravnos","name":"Ravnos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar15944_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"151"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-26T04:29:18-08:00","id":1170646,"title":"","content":"This is something I've headcanoned since I got into WtA, and it is pretty anime in a sense, but I thought others could use this still.<br /> <br /> In WoD, humans, wolves and most other species with shifter ties, have eye and hair colours than they lack in our world. Due to the constant changing of genes and traits that happens when shifters breed over a millenia if not more, humans for example can have plain yellow or orange eyes and they are not seen as strange. Wolves can have blood red coats, stark black and white coats and so on. These are just common traits and in fact do not imply kinfolk status. Just that somewhere in that person's heritage, there was a garou.<br /> <br /> Note that even if someone had blood red hair and yellow eyes and had a Red Talon grandfather, they would not be kin to the tribe. The totem decides who gets to be kin.<br /> <br /> Another thing is that garou genes have spread so far and so wide, that garou can pop up from nearly any family. Most non-purebred garou come from these lost lines, while the more purebreed you have the more you were expected to know of the Nation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-27T09:41:06-08:00","id":1170974,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1101014-w-ta-the-house-canon-thread-what-s-true-at-your-table?p=1170646#post1170646\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is something I've headcanoned since I got into WtA, and it is pretty anime in a sense, but I thought others could use this still.<br /> <br /> In WoD, humans, wolves and most other species with shifter ties, have eye and hair colours than they lack in our world. Due to the constant changing of genes and traits that happens when shifters breed over a millenia if not more, humans for example can have plain yellow or orange eyes and they are not seen as strange. Wolves can have blood red coats, stark black and white coats and so on. These are just common traits and in fact do not imply kinfolk status. Just that somewhere in that person's heritage, there was a garou.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm clearly going to have to use that if I ever get to run a Rage Across Japan game. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-04T01:28:09-08:00","id":1173176,"title":"","content":"- Sense Wyrm is just Sense Bane. It can detect Fomori (since there is a Bane in there), but it doesn't detect unpossessed servants of the Wyrm (including BSDs). Conflicting views about what are and what are not &quot;of the Wyrm&quot; permeates conflicts among the Gaian Tribes, as well as facilitates events like the Second War of Rage.<br /> <br /> - If Pentex actually owned its many so-called &quot;Subsidiaries&quot; it would be impossible to hide its status as one of the largest and most powerful corporations on the planet. It doesn't own them. It is invested in many of them, but largely works an industrial supplier, and realtor. In this role it coordinates other independent servants of the Wyrm, props up potential agents, and gets a foot in the door to corrupt. But any status it has as the Wyrm's most direct corporate servants, acting as cultic mediators between Earth &amp; Malfeas to these other companies, is entirely off the books - they do not own majority shares for all of these major players in their respective industries.<br /> <br /> - Children of Gaia are not a Tribe. I might feel differently if they got a decent Revised-quality Tribe Book, but they didn't, so I simply do not have a sense of them as a culture like I do the other Tribes. Instead, they exist as a multi-Tribal camp dedicated to inter-tribal peace, equality, restoring relations with the Fera, and opposing all war not directly against the Wyrm itself as feeding the Beast-of-War.<br /> <br /> - Black Tooth still lives. He and his Pride dominate southeast Africa and he names himself King of Cats. While his brutality toward all who would oppose him is horrific, he is also actually fighting the Wyrm's minions. The Ahadi exists as a resistance movement against him, but many who may hate him are reluctant to throw their support behind it because he is seen as an effective commander against the Wyrm.<br /> <br /> - Yava are largely metaphoric (I have a list of what they all actually mean), but work in many ways like &quot;True Names&quot; of the Tribe. If a Bastet knows their Tribe's Yava they are virtually immune to mind-reading and mental-influence supernatural powers from someone who does not know their Yava. If someone discovers a Tribe's Yava, members of that Tribe can not even exert the normal defensive rolls or willpower expenditures against mind-reading or supernatural mental-influences.<br /> <br /> - The Silver Crown is still missing (I'm thinking of throwing the Tribes into chaos via the &quot;Rightful King&quot; being revealed to be a Metis); Jonas Albrecht does not exist as an NPC (he's clearly someone's PC, as opposed to characters like Konetziko who comes of more as an interesting plot hook for pcs to interact with).<br /> <br /> - &quot;Lunatics&quot; do actually go through the First Change, they just completely reject their nature, and as a result cannot control their shifting, generally only doing it in Frenzy under their Auspice moon. They are in short Classic Hollywood Werewolves.<br /> <br /> - The Beast Courts are less idyllic. After all, look at the ecological disaster that is modern China - clearly not a sign they have their shit together. They are very hierarchical, and the survival of the Zhong Lung is a closely guarded secret. Generally, the Nezumi, Tengu, and any Bagheera or Garou who join have no idea, with the upper ranks of the Courts they're aware of being dominated by Khan, Same-Bito, and Kitsune, who in turn are aware of the Zhong Lung above them. Naga keep to the shadows and pass themselves off as Zhong Lung to the upper Courts when they have to.<br /> <br /> -Normal Ananasi exist in East Asia and obviously hate the Kumo.<br /> <br /> [more later]","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":1098,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","user":"glamourweaver","date":". 01-04-2018, 05:00 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-04T17:58:16-08:00","id":1173384,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1101014-w-ta-the-house-canon-thread-what-s-true-at-your-table?p=1173176#post1173176\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">- If Pentex actually owned its many so-called &quot;Subsidiaries&quot; it would be impossible to hide its status as one of the largest and most powerful corporations on the planet. It doesn't own them. It is invested in many of them,</div> </div> </div> </div>That is, IIRC, the way it is presented in Subsidiaries. PENTEX is a holding company, owning outstanding stock in a huge range of businesses, either directly or through various fronts. Those businesses are usually already pretty corrupt in their own right in some way or another before even coming to PENTEX's attention (Magadon being founded by a biological warfare specialist who never quite gave that line of research up, for example, or Ardus likely being owned by the mob), and PENTEX finds ways to make them feed off of each other to create more money and more corruption. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-04T19:13:12-08:00","id":1173397,"title":"","content":"I had understood a \u201cHolding Company\u201d as implying a controlling interest, which is what I was suggesting Pentex does not have. But if I misunderstood the concept, then yeah I\u2019m cool with the canon presentation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-05T12:42:24-08:00","id":1173549,"title":"","content":"Well, keep in mind that a lot of early White Wolf/Werewolf/PENTEX stuff was written by people whose understanding of &quot;modern&quot; (and by that I mean early 90s) business probably consisted entirely of the movies Wall Street and Robocop, and Mr. Burns on the Simpsons, and at times was aimed more at parody than horror. So it's horribly wonky in a number of places, and sometimes requires fiddling. Revised edition fixed some of this, but never really in enough detail or space.<br /> <br /> I, personally, run PENTEX a little grittier than what's presented in some of the source material. Part of that involves doing a lot of research into the history and practices of the different industries involved, which can be fascinating (both in the &quot;that's really interesting&quot; sense and the &quot;is that a train wreck up ahead?&quot; sense). It's also pretty cool when you can find preexisting takes on certain things that are even creepier than the Werewolf versions. For example, my version of Avalon Toys takes a massive amount of inspiration from a short piece Grant Morrison did for Vertigo's WEIRD WAR TALES miniseries called (IIRC) &quot;The New Toys&quot;, and if PENTEX's BoD ever found out what the company was <i>really</i> up to, they'd likely try to burn it to the ground.<br /> <br /> I still lament that there was never a book devoted entire to PENTEX as a whole, preferably presenting it as an onion whose layers have to be pulled back by the PCs and the Garou Nation, starting with how normal mundane businesses and industries function in the WoD and exactly why their normal everyday non-Wyrm corrupted activities are still a threat to the Garou and their interests, continuing down into the various PENTEX subsidiary holdings and what they do, then to PENTEX itself and it's special projects of creating First Team super soldiers, psychic weapons, and other craziness as part of their plan for ultimate power.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-06T13:40:19-08:00","id":1173825,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I\u2019m struggling a bit with the elements I\u2019d want to use Pentex Subsidiaries to talk about at my table, vs those elements that are really stupid conspiracy theories I don\u2019t want to reinforce...<br /> <br /> Take Megadon<br /> <br /> Real issues:<br /> - Profiting off of opioid addiction<br /> - Supporing marijuana criminalized status and the war on drugs to help maintain industry control of pain relief<br /> - price gouging the desperate<br /> <br /> Bullshit conspiracy theories:<br /> - Anti-Vaxx nonsense<br /> - Scientology fueled anti-Psychiatry nonsense","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-06T23:12:40-08:00","id":1173968,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1101014-w-ta-the-house-canon-thread-what-s-true-at-your-table?p=1173176#post1173176\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> - Children of Gaia are not a Tribe. I might feel differently if they got a decent Revised-quality Tribe Book, but they didn't, so I simply do not have a sense of them as a culture like I do the other Tribes. Instead, they exist as a multi-Tribal camp dedicated to inter-tribal peace, equality, restoring relations with the Fera, and opposing all war not directly against the Wyrm itself as feeding the Beast-of-War.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Have you considered making them a Pan-breed camp? I Feel like there could be an interesting contrast as an attempt at &quot;Universalist&quot; vs highly human cultured attempts at pan breed organizations.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-07T01:38:40-08:00","id":1173979,"title":"","content":"I think they\u2019re open to becoming that, but it hasn\u2019t happened yet, because they\u2019re still working on building those bridges. They\u2019re still in the olive branch stage to the Fera. Going multi-Breed is something PCs at my table would be capable of making happen.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-07T12:49:40-08:00","id":1174114,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1101014-w-ta-the-house-canon-thread-what-s-true-at-your-table?p=1173979#post1173979\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think they\u2019re open to becoming that, but it hasn\u2019t happened yet, because they\u2019re still working on building those bridges. They\u2019re still in the olive branch stage to the Fera. Going multi-Breed is something PCs at my table would be capable of making happen.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I was thinking that since your Emerald Court variant has taken up a more Confucian tone(thus potentially pushing htem more weavery) an interesting counter group in the area that tries to push more towards &quot;as the emerald mother intended&quot; without throwing out cross breed connectiosn would be interesting as a political flare up.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-07T12:53:18-08:00","id":1174115,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1101014-w-ta-the-house-canon-thread-what-s-true-at-your-table?p=1174114#post1174114\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I was thinking that since your Emerald Court variant has taken up a more Confucian tone(thus potentially pushing htem more weavery) an interesting counter group in the area that tries to push more towards &quot;as the emerald mother intended&quot; without throwing out cross breed connectiosn would be interesting as a political flare up.</div> </div> </div> </div>Beings with Rage can only be so Confucian before they snap. The Hakken are already at an extreme that probably can't go any further, and they have to make lots of allowances for not being human.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-07T13:55:49-08:00","id":1174126,"title":"","content":"My take on the Children of Gaia has always been that their goal is to unify the Garou Nation <i>under their own leadership</i>, in a way that could be stereotyped/trivialized as &quot;we want everyone to live together in peace, love and harmony, and will eagerly engage in passive aggressive bullying tactics against anyone who doesn't think the way we do&quot;, but more honestly is probably based around the sincere belief that things for the Garou Nation started going downhill when they first divided into tribes. Over all, their modus operandi is that a) it's possible to resolve internal Garou vs Garou conflicts with ways other than unrestrained violence and b) when dealing with outside enemies, especially those corrupted by the Wyrm, it's ethically worthwhile to at least investigate the potential for redemption or healing before taking the option of putting a creature out of its misery through mercy killing. In the sense of the Garou Nation as a whole, they're one of the four leadership tribes (along with the Silver Fangs, Shadow Lords and Croatan), and should be viewed by the first two as potential rivals.<br /> <br /> My take on the Beast Courts was that it's a bunch of people who don't like each other for a wide number of reasons who are only able to co-exist because of a very strict adherence to carefully detailed rules of etiquette everyone grudgingly agreed upon. (But then I also have the Asian Guhral still around and the Nagah a rare oddity in the courts, so I am weird.)<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":12890,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","user":"No One of Consequence","date":". 01-07-2018, 05:00 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-08T18:37:47-08:00","id":1174425,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1101014-w-ta-the-house-canon-thread-what-s-true-at-your-table?p=1173549#post1173549\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">my version of Avalon Toys takes a massive amount of inspiration from a short piece Grant Morrison did for Vertigo's WEIRD WAR TALES miniseries called (IIRC) &amp;quot;The New Toys&amp;quot;, and if PENTEX's BoD ever found out what the company was <i>really</i> up to, they'd likely try to burn it to the ground.</div> </div> </div> </div>I\u2019d love to hear more about this!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-09T13:11:59-08:00","id":1174626,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1101014-w-ta-the-house-canon-thread-what-s-true-at-your-table?p=1174425#post1174425\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I\u2019d love to hear more about this!</div> </div> </div> </div>I really hate to spoil it, because the first time I read it, the final reveal is kind of creepy. Basically, it's told from the POV of a GI Joe figure, one of the old 1960s versions, who has only known an unrelenting world of endless war between his side and the other. He get's &quot;captured&quot; by a little girl and ends up inside, as a male companion for a Barbie, and enjoys this strange new existence (in spite of the occasional weirdness of being put in a dress and make up). Then one day apparently Barbie is replaced by ... something, and when he realizes the scope of what's going on, he runs back to his old unit, seeking help and trying to warn them of this threat. He's promptly executed for desertion, all while screaming about the danger of the new toys. It ends with a final splash page of <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">the little girl in her bed asleep, followed by another page of the same shot, but all the toys are these insectoid style alien things.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> So, yeah, my version of Avalon Toys is that <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">they're run by <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Insect_from_Shaggai\" target=\"_blank\">the Insects from Shaggai</a> </div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":12890,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","user":"No One of Consequence","date":". 01-09-2018, 04:18 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-09T13:22:23-08:00","id":1174630,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1101014-w-ta-the-house-canon-thread-what-s-true-at-your-table?p=1174626#post1174626\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> So, yeah, my version of Avalon Toys is that <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">they're run by <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Insect_from_Shaggai\" target=\"_blank\">the Insects from Shaggai</a> </div></div> </div> </div></div> </div> </div> </div>Motherfuck.<br /> <br /> Now I'll never look at all of my Marvel Legends figures the same...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">&quot;Steel isn't strong, boy. Flesh is stronger.&quot;</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/95-fat-larry","name":"Fat Larry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar95_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-16T08:50:31-08:00","id":1176528,"title":"","content":"Was talking with a friend how it would be cool to explore the setting as the Garou have been so depopulated that by the modern day there's not enough left to form these global tribes. I could see in the tribal homelands there's enough echoes for influence and such, but for the most part the last few septs are some elders and maybe a pack or two. You could really emphasize the apocalyptic nature of the struggle, and the cultural loss and disintegration werewolf society faces.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":21481,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/21481-onkwe","user":"Onkwe","date":". 01-16-2018, 12:00 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/21481-onkwe","name":"Onkwe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar21481_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"162"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-16T10:40:47-08:00","id":1176543,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Onkwe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1101014-w-ta-the-house-canon-thread-what-s-true-at-your-table?p=1176528#post1176528\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Was talking with a friend how it would be cool to explore the setting as the Garou have been so depopulated that by the modern day there's not enough left to form these global tribes. I could see in the tribal homelands there's enough echoes for influence and such, but for the most part the last few septs are some elders and maybe a pack or two. You could really emphasize the apocalyptic nature of the struggle, and the cultural loss and disintegration werewolf society faces.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm doing something similar now.<br /> <br /> One of the things I've begun changing about my setting is that I'm lowering the population of the Garou, and decreasing the number of high ranking caerns (there's only maybe a dozen rank 5 caerns left in the world for all the Changing Breeds, and perhaps twice that number of rank 4). I've also increased the number of Ronin in the game - collectively they would be the largest &quot;tribe&quot;. Combined with the above, this really thins out the number of actual Garou.<br /> <br /> There are definitely still tribes - since all you need is the Rite of Passage to get your tribal totem - but there is the idea that the heritage of the Garou is being lost. Learning rites, various lore, the Litany in its long form, and other Garou or tribal heritage becomes a task in itself and involves people travelling to different septs, finding Old Ones, and making a real effort to learn these.<br /> <br /> I've found a lower population is more likely to result in the kind of stories/plots/encounters I like to have than the default population found in the sourcebooks or games I've played in. I like games that are recognizably in the horror genre and characters reminiscent of actual werewolves found in stories elsewhere, than the epic fantasy genre the game devolves into and which canon tends to encourage.<br /> <br /> I like politics to be between septs, and low ranking septs are more understandably monotribal. And the decreased population and resources available heightens conflicts between Garou. And the less Garou population encourages the idea that the Garou simply don't swarm over their enemies and defeat them in detail. In turn, I can make their foes more subtle and hidden, less over the top. More like cultists in Call of Cthulhu games than the Wyrm factions in the source material. By toning down the number of supernatural creatures, the game seems more believable to me.<br /> <br /> Since PCs are likely to want to be in multitribal packs, I need to make some concessions so packs often start out in relatively rare rank 3 (or a few overpopulated rank 2) caerns, but the characters will know that most caerns out there are only rank 1 and 2.<br /> <br /> This has only been slowly forming in my mind over the past year so I haven't run this revised version of my setting in any chronicle, but this is the direction I am currently going in.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3046,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","user":"Black Fox","date":". 01-16-2018, 01:54 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-23T12:44:09-08:00","id":1178511,"title":"","content":"Garou matings are sterile.Metis are born from Garou and Spirits coupling. They are still deformed and sterile and most Garou still find them disturbing enough to despise them.<br /> <br /> A sizeable minority of Homid Shifters come from sheltered Kinfolk communities who don't officialy exist on any census. How the Garou and the Fera treat these communities range from &quot;benevolent rule&quot; to &quot;Black Spiral levels of depravity<br /> <br /> The War of Rage was less successful than in canon, the Changing Breeds were weakened to the point of not influencing history but the Garou know they survived. Doesn't make the world much less fucked.<br /> <br /> The White Howlers didn't fall to the Wyrm even if 40% of the Tribe including most of the elders did. The Black Spirals have but a few Hives and most are found as a dark elite in Wyrmish Cults. Gatherings of more than three packs are cause of terrible concern for the septs aware of it.<br /> <br /> Most Werewolves devoted to the Wyrm never dance the Black Spiral but remain as cankers among their people, slowly tryiing to corrupt them. Dancing the Spiral is considered a reward as it strengthen you but a bitter one for you are unable to meaningfully infiltrate Ga\u00efan septs again.<br /> <br /> The Garou Nation is the name given to a group of werewolf protectorates in Europe. The others great groups are the Protectorate of the Silver Crown in America, the Amabeth in the Amazon, the Ahadi in Africa and the Beast Courts in Asia. They don't like each other very much.<br /> <br /> Members of the Triat do not &quot;want&quot; things in the manner a mortal mind may understand. Below them are a pantheon of Celestines who fight or ignore each other. One of the Weaver Celestines is the Mother of the Pattern Spiders and she would want a world where everything happens according to natural cycles. She is opposed by the Machine-God who is the &quot;face&quot; of the Weaver this day.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2225,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2225-ganonso","user":"ganonso","date":". 01-23-2018, 03:47 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2225-ganonso","name":"ganonso","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2225_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-23T13:02:59-08:00","id":1178517,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ganonso</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1101014-w-ta-the-house-canon-thread-what-s-true-at-your-table?p=1178511#post1178511\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Members of the Triat do not &amp;quot;want&amp;quot; things in the manner a mortal mind may understand. Below them are a pantheon of Celestines who fight or ignore each other. One of the Weaver Celestines is the Mother of the Pattern Spiders and she would want a world where everything happens according to natural cycles. She is opposed by the Machine-God who is the &amp;quot;face&amp;quot; of the Weaver this day.</div> </div> </div> </div>Does the Mother replace Queen Ananasa in your cosmology, or are they otherwise differentiated?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-23T13:39:16-08:00","id":1178535,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1101014-w-ta-the-house-canon-thread-what-s-true-at-your-table?p=1178517#post1178517\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Does the Mother replace Queen Ananasa in your cosmology, or are they otherwise differentiated?</div> </div> </div> </div>They are different. I more or less understood that Ananasa ahd the spirits that created the Fera were Incarnae not Celestines. Anansa in my games is still in her opal prison plotting to release the Wyrm from its torment.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2225-ganonso","name":"ganonso","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2225_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-23T14:12:30-08:00","id":1178548,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ganonso</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1101014-w-ta-the-house-canon-thread-what-s-true-at-your-table?p=1178535#post1178535\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> They are different. I more or less understood that Ananasa ahd the spirits that created the Fera were Incarnae not Celestines. Anansa in my games is still in her opal prison plotting to release the Wyrm from its torment.</div> </div> </div> </div>Fair enough. I was more referring to how she represents the type of order the Weaver originally represented before going mad, which sounded like your description of the Mother of Pattern Spiders.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-23T14:51:40-08:00","id":1178561,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1101014-w-ta-the-house-canon-thread-what-s-true-at-your-table?p=1178548#post1178548\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Fair enough. I was more referring to how she represents the type of order the Weaver originally represented before going mad, which sounded like your description of the Mother of Pattern Spiders.</div> </div> </div> </div>I see. Unfortunately the Mother of Pattern-Spiders is as insane as the other Weaver Celestines. Humanity you see is disrupting the natural order with thier innovation and their chaotic natures and their capacity to evolve in unpredictable ways. And wasn't this free-will thing an error?<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2225-ganonso","name":"ganonso","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2225_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-23T16:00:31-08:00","id":1178583,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ganonso</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1101014-w-ta-the-house-canon-thread-what-s-true-at-your-table?p=1178561#post1178561\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I see. Unfortunately the Mother of Pattern-Spiders is as insane as the other Weaver Celestines. Humanity you see is disrupting the natural order with thier innovation and their chaotic natures and their capacity to evolve in unpredictable ways. And wasn't this free-will thing an error?<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, that\u2019s interesting, cool!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-24T06:46:00-08:00","id":1178763,"title":"","content":"Here are my Children of Ga\u00efa<br /> <br /> <br /> There are some who think the Children of Ga\u00efa are the tribe of peace, a tribe of cowards who are just good to throw wild parties and moan about non-violence while the others do all the work. This is false. All Garou rage against something and the Children of Ga\u00efa cry against the death of innocence, against the defilement of what was pure and the monsters of the world being free to walk among the sheep. They consider themselves Ga\u00efa chosen priests and some indeed walk the human world seeking to evangelize. Unlike some could think they teach the truth of nature as it is, red in tooth and claws and how cooperation and trust are the best strategy to fight the darkness. Among the Garou their words are the same but there they use their expertise as healers to make themselves indispensable. When comes the times to fight, rare is the Child of Ga\u00efa foolish enough to try to redeem some Wyrmish cultist on the field, they favor beheading strikes proving Ga\u00efa\u2019s own superiority against the best the foe has to offer. They consider these cults and sects dedicated to the Corruptor as their favorite prey. They are servants of Unicorn and their ban is \u201cPay Each Garou in Kind\u201d Basically they are not the hippie tribes but the Cleric/Paladin's tribe. They treat Ga\u00efa with zealous devotion and while they consider that indeed the war is first won in the hearts and minds of others, they are not adverse to have the claws out. Their faults are self-righteousness beyond the other Garou, an unspoken belief unity means they are in charge, and downright cult behaviour when interacting with humanity. Thoughts?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2225,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2225-ganonso","user":"ganonso","date":". 01-24-2018, 09:54 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2225-ganonso","name":"ganonso","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2225_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-24T06:46:31-08:00","id":1178764,"title":"","content":"I have never been bothered with the metaplot. <br /> The garou aren't good guys, they're terrorist vigilantes with delusions, tricked by spirits and their own egos into thinking they're doing something noble. The garou are notably terrible at telling apart wyld spirits from wyrm ones, and there's a line between bane and wyrmy spirit that they usually don't understand. Garou are tribals at heart, and the conflict between them is ramped up. Truly, the garou are more a tale of former kings reacting badly to a world they once ruled turning away from them, finding common cause with &quot;gaian&quot; spirits who want to look out for themselves as man shrinks their territory. The nation wants something to be done, the spirals have accepted their course. <br /> I really hide this viewpoint from my players though, I tell them the lies like I want them to believe them. <br /> <br /> I've thought out the many, many ways in which pentex can be an apocalyptic cult and a business with poor ethics. If they were just the former, the world would be over, if they were just the latter, the garou wouldn't have any more beef with them than they would anything else. I've thought of the myriad of ways in which they could make profits (let's be honest, if you had to recruit so many security personal and first teams just to defend your stuff, you might as well just not pollute) <br /> All garou, allies excluded, and other unnatural entities are to be harvested for parts, they have incredibly high value to occultists,private collectors and a few science corps. Metis are especially valuable some will pay millions just for a single claw. <br /> Waste dumps and such, beyond defiling caerns to move garou out permanently, is the price that pays for bane investments and business. Nobody goes out of their way to polute for the lulz. On the same note, tainting products is done to make people more dependent on them, or to confuse garou, or on the whims of banes who offer rewards, people becoming assholes because they drink blue stripe is just a happy sideaffect. Now the important part to this is that, while i've yet to have a player in a position for this temptation, I would completely set this system up for players to use. <br /> There are nephandi within certain subisdiaries that make some of the more advanced technologies. There's some small overlap with mage, though pentex is far behind the technocracy. <br /> The other wyrm elements are made just as prominent as balefire, even though balefire is insanely cool. I've considered something for metal, glass and lightning, but I've yet to implement them.<br /> The frog changers were initially failures, but subsequent attempts provided a more successful rendition of the breed, for use in aquatic support. They are more reliable and loyal. <br /> A lot of the stuff that pentex makes to kill garou actually ends up in very exclusive sales, for no less than two and a half million USD, you too can have your very own war wolf! You can also hire a first team or even make you and a buddy a formori (it's advertised way better,of course)! On the flipside, Pentex subsidiaries have been known to get a hold of old HIT marks, and they long for many of the cloning and weapon technologies their weaver rivals possess. <br /> <b>I really, really want to write a book for a pentex game.</b> <br /> <br /> Does anyone know much about importing things from scar or that cyber hell? How viable is plundering the spirit world for resources?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Be correct.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23728-pewpew","name":"PewPew","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"107"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-24T06:48:56-08:00","id":1178765,"title":"","content":"EDIT: Accidental Double post","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2225,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2225-ganonso","user":"ganonso","date":". 01-24-2018, 09:52 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2225-ganonso","name":"ganonso","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2225_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-24T09:09:46-08:00","id":1178818,"title":"","content":"<b>How the Red Talons fell</b><br /> <br /> <i>They were sure it was going to be the Wyrm, that would take the tribe of Griffin in the end. After all, with their unbridled Rage and their desperate hatered towards humanity, it was all but a given. Still, some theorized that it could as easily be the Wyld that would turn them into its gorgons.<br /> <br /> Some cynical ragabash even suggested the Weaver, given the Talons rarely changed their ways.<br /> <br /> Yet, when the first rabid wolves in crinos attacked humans and could not be reasoned with even by Garou Tongue, the Garou Nation was faced with another possibility they had ignored as impossible. Garou who were known to be Elder ranked suddenly sought Uktena, Fury and Wendigo septs as cubs, holding no trace of any purebreed. Yet their pelts wered the blood-red of the Talons. Packs following Griffon suddenly had their totem change into something similar but not quite.<br /> <br /> A questing pack was sent to the Red Talon homelands to find out the reason for the sudden disappearances of Griffon. The pack found a realm filled with ancestor spirits and everything seemed as usual, but it felt empty in some way. Storm-Chaser, a recent ancestor explained to the pack the reason with a bitter tone.<br /> <br /> &quot;The new cubs aren't like us anymore. They have Rage, but they no longer think or see the future. They have only wolf-hearts and no human minds. Griffon cannot be a totem of wolves, he needs garou, so he left us&quot;<br /> <br /> As the pack returned with the news, a deep fear descended upon the Nation. The Red Talons had lost their human side, who knew if the opposite was possible.</i><br /> <br /> <br /> --<br /> <br /> Basically, an interesting twist to the typical 'tribe falls' scenario. Please note that Red Talons lost their humanity through quite a bit of effort on their part, Glass Walkers cannot lose their humanity by simply being human based. It takes willing ignorance to go that route.<br /> <br /> The semi-garou the new garou of Talon breeding became are basically wolves that can shift when extremely nervous/afraid. They mostly take hispo, some may take crinos. Homid and glabro are beyond them. They have trouble shifting back and often they can end up living the rest of their short lives in these forms. They have Rage, but it is alien and frightening to them and other wolves.<br /> <br /> Luckily, this loss of humanity is only found among Red Talon garou and kin. It is a limited number of pairings that can result in a semi-garou, but that alone spelt the doom for the Talons as a tribe.<br /> <br /> What does this mean for the Nation? Well, first of all, fear.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-24T09:18:20-08:00","id":1178823,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1101014-w-ta-the-house-canon-thread-what-s-true-at-your-table?p=1178818#post1178818\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>How the Red Talons fell</b><br /> <br /> <i>They were sure it was going to be the Wyrm, that would take the tribe of Griffin in the end. After all, with their unbridled Rage and their desperate hatered towards humanity, it was all but a given. Still, some theorized that it could as easily be the Wyld that would turn them into its gorgons.<br /> <br /> Some cynical ragabash even suggested the Weaver, given the Talons rarely changed their ways.<br /> <br /> Yet, when the first rabid wolves in crinos attacked humans and could not be reasoned with even by Garou Tongue, the Garou Nation was faced with another possibility they had ignored as impossible. Garou who were known to be Elder ranked suddenly sought Uktena, Fury and Wendigo septs as cubs, holding no trace of any purebreed. Yet their pelts wered the blood-red of the Talons. Packs following Griffon suddenly had their totem change into something similar but not quite.<br /> <br /> A questing pack was sent to the Red Talon homelands to find out the reason for the sudden disappearances of Griffon. The pack found a realm filled with ancestor spirits and everything seemed as usual, but it felt empty in some way. Storm-Chaser, a recent ancestor explained to the pack the reason with a bitter tone.<br /> <br /> &quot;The new cubs aren't like us anymore. They have Rage, but they no longer think or see the future. They have only wolf-hearts and no human minds. Griffon cannot be a totem of wolves, he needs garou, so he left us&quot;<br /> <br /> As the pack returned with the news, a deep fear descended upon the Nation. The Red Talons had lost their human side, who knew if the opposite was possible.</i><br /> <br /> <br /> --<br /> <br /> Basically, an interesting twist to the typical 'tribe falls' scenario. Please note that Red Talons lost their humanity through quite a bit of effort on their part, Glass Walkers cannot lose their humanity by simply being human based. It takes willing ignorance to go that route.<br /> <br /> The semi-garou the new garou of Talon breeding became are basically wolves that can shift when extremely nervous/afraid. They mostly take hispo, some may take crinos. Homid and glabro are beyond them. They have trouble shifting back and often they can end up living the rest of their short lives in these forms. They have Rage, but it is alien and frightening to them and other wolves.<br /> <br /> Luckily, this loss of humanity is only found among Red Talon garou and kin. It is a limited number of pairings that can result in a semi-garou, but that alone spelt the doom for the Talons as a tribe.<br /> <br /> What does this mean for the Nation? Well, first of all, fear.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nice idea but considering Lupus have the highest Gnosis of the Breeds would your semi-Garou be only physical creatures or be able to step-sideways or bargain with spirits? Which would creep the Garou even more as the Talons would become way more dangerous than simply animals who can shift in Crinos.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2225-ganonso","name":"ganonso","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2225_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-24T09:26:27-08:00","id":1178826,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ganonso</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1101014-w-ta-the-house-canon-thread-what-s-true-at-your-table?p=1178823#post1178823\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Nice idea but considering Lupus have the highest Gnosis of the Breeds would your semi-Garou be only physical creatures or be able to step-sideways or bargain with spirits? Which would creep the Garou even more as the Talons would become way more dangerous than simply animals who can shift in Crinos.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>In my opinion, in order to step sideways, you need to have a mind that is capable of thinking beyond this world and understanding that there is more to this world than senses and time. I myself don't much like the lupus 5 gnosis, because it treats the senses of a creature as tied to understanding the supernatural. Sure, it should be a -bit- higher than with homids, but to me it makes wolves sound noble needlesly.<br /> <br /> So,no, the semi-garou cannot step sideways, they are basically remnants of what Talons once were.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Basically, humans can become enlightened and cross the gauntlet, animals can't. That's the short of it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":110,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","user":"Ana Mizuki","date":". 01-24-2018, 12:38 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-30T13:45:11-08:00","id":1180873,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1101014-w-ta-the-house-canon-thread-what-s-true-at-your-table?p=1176543#post1176543\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm doing something similar now.<br /> <br /> One of the things I've begun changing about my setting is that I'm lowering the population of the Garou, and decreasing the number of high ranking caerns (there's only maybe a dozen rank 5 caerns left in the world for all the Changing Breeds, and perhaps twice that number of rank 4). I've also increased the number of Ronin in the game - collectively they would be the largest &amp;quot;tribe&amp;quot;. Combined with the above, this really thins out the number of actual Garou.<br /> <br /> There are definitely still tribes - since all you need is the Rite of Passage to get your tribal totem - but there is the idea that the heritage of the Garou is being lost. Learning rites, various lore, the Litany in its long form, and other Garou or tribal heritage becomes a task in itself and involves people travelling to different septs, finding Old Ones, and making a real effort to learn these.<br /> <br /> I've found a lower population is more likely to result in the kind of stories/plots/encounters I like to have than the default population found in the sourcebooks or games I've played in. I like games that are recognizably in the horror genre and characters reminiscent of actual werewolves found in stories elsewhere, than the epic fantasy genre the game devolves into and which canon tends to encourage.<br /> <br /> I like politics to be between septs, and low ranking septs are more understandably monotribal. And the decreased population and resources available heightens conflicts between Garou. And the less Garou population encourages the idea that the Garou simply don't swarm over their enemies and defeat them in detail. In turn, I can make their foes more subtle and hidden, less over the top. More like cultists in Call of Cthulhu games than the Wyrm factions in the source material. By toning down the number of supernatural creatures, the game seems more believable to me.<br /> <br /> Since PCs are likely to want to be in multitribal packs, I need to make some concessions so packs often start out in relatively rare rank 3 (or a few overpopulated rank 2) caerns, but the characters will know that most caerns out there are only rank 1 and 2.<br /> <br /> This has only been slowly forming in my mind over the past year so I haven't run this revised version of my setting in any chronicle, but this is the direction I am currently going in.</div> </div> </div> </div>I like this, but I tend to draw more on folklore, myths, and rl religions when recreating the Wyrm. Lovecraftian stuff is cool though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/21481-onkwe","name":"Onkwe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar21481_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"162"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-30T15:01:51-08:00","id":1180893,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Onkwe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1101014-w-ta-the-house-canon-thread-what-s-true-at-your-table?p=1180873#post1180873\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I like this, but I tend to draw more on folklore, myths, and rl religions when recreating the Wyrm. Lovecraftian stuff is cool though.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Hellboy/BPRD comic books do an excellent job of combining myth, legend, religion, Lovecraft, and many other horror styles together. It blends very well despite each kind of horror genre being very different from each other. I try to mimic that as much I can in my own Werewolf chronicles, but with varying degrees of success.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-30T15:34:32-08:00","id":1180902,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1101014-w-ta-the-house-canon-thread-what-s-true-at-your-table?p=1180893#post1180893\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The Hellboy/BPRD comic books do an excellent job of combining myth, legend, religion, Lovecraft, and many other horror styles together. It blends very well despite each kind of horror genre being very different from each other. I try to mimic that as much I can in my own Werewolf chronicles, but with varying degrees of success.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Awesome. Hellboy is definetly a major inspiration for a lot of WoD stuff, and how it mixes all that together. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/21481-onkwe","name":"Onkwe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar21481_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"162"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-31T03:43:26-08:00","id":1181067,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/21481-onkwe\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar21481_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"21481\" data-vbnamecard=\"21481\">Onkwe</a> How do you handle rites and such in your games? Are they area/culture specific in their functions?<br /> <br /> For me, just going by Finnish culture and what animism I know of my country's history, at least Rite of Cleansing is generally very sombre and focuses much more on water and washing away the filth. This usually manifests as a trip to the sauna in very hot conditions and a lot of beating of the taint by branches for garou/people. For objects, usually near a lake and washed with the lake's own water while singing spells.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-31T08:34:45-08:00","id":1181140,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1101014-w-ta-the-house-canon-thread-what-s-true-at-your-table?p=1181067#post1181067\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/21481-onkwe\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar21481_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"21481\" data-vbnamecard=\"21481\">Onkwe</a> How do you handle rites and such in your games? Are they area/culture specific in their functions?<br /> <br /> For me, just going by Finnish culture and what animism I know of my country's history, at least Rite of Cleansing is generally very sombre and focuses much more on water and washing away the filth. This usually manifests as a trip to the sauna in very hot conditions and a lot of beating of the taint by branches for garou/people. For objects, usually near a lake and washed with the lake's own water while singing spells.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> It depends on the Tribe(s) of a sept and the specific region of the world.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/21481-onkwe","name":"Onkwe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar21481_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"162"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-31T08:38:26-08:00","id":1181141,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Onkwe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1101014-w-ta-the-house-canon-thread-what-s-true-at-your-table?p=1181140#post1181140\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> It depends on the Tribe(s) of a sept and the specific region of the world.</div> </div> </div> </div>Cool, could you give me an example, if you want to?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-31T08:49:51-08:00","id":1181148,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1101014-w-ta-the-house-canon-thread-what-s-true-at-your-table?p=1181141#post1181141\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Cool, could you give me an example, if you want to?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Like an example for a Wendigo version of the Rite of Cleansing would largely involve smudging oneself, an object, or area with sage and/or ceder, using a feather to direct the smoke. She or he would keep their thoughts positive and humble through the whole process, not blow on the smoldering medicines, and letting them burn out naturally.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/21481-onkwe","name":"Onkwe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar21481_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"162"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-31T14:19:23-08:00","id":1181231,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1101014-w-ta-the-house-canon-thread-what-s-true-at-your-table?p=1178818#post1178818\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>How the Red Talons fell</b><br /> <br /> <i>They were sure it was going to be the Wyrm, that would take the tribe of Griffin in the end. After all, with their unbridled Rage and their desperate hatered towards humanity, it was all but a given. Still, some theorized that it could as easily be the Wyld that would turn them into its gorgons.<br /> <br /> Some cynical ragabash even suggested the Weaver, given the Talons rarely changed their ways.</i><br /> <br /> ...<br /> Please note that Red Talons lost their humanity through quite a bit of effort on their part, Glass Walkers cannot lose their humanity by simply being human based. It takes willing ignorance to go that route.<br /> <br /> The semi-garou the new garou of Talon breeding became are basically wolves that can shift when extremely nervous/afraid. They mostly take hispo, some may take crinos. Homid and glabro are beyond them. They have trouble shifting back and often they can end up living the rest of their short lives in these forms. They have Rage, but it is alien and frightening to them and other wolves.<br /> <br /> Luckily, this loss of humanity is only found among Red Talon garou and kin. It is a limited number of pairings that can result in a semi-garou, but that alone spelt the doom for the Talons as a tribe.<br /> <br /> What does this mean for the Nation? Well, first of all, fear.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sub-sentient hispo and crinos werewolves roaming the wilderness would be a severe threat to the Veil!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13713-wilson","name":"Wilson","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"182"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-31T15:23:51-08:00","id":1181244,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wilson</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1101014-w-ta-the-house-canon-thread-what-s-true-at-your-table?p=1181231#post1181231\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Sub-sentient hispo and crinos werewolves roaming the wilderness would be a severe threat to the Veil!</div> </div> </div> </div>Heck yeah it is, hence why it is a legit issue for the garou to take them down. That is the terrible thing about the fall of the Talons, the results are creatures without control and sense that die quickly or are captured by BSDs.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-01T05:17:37-08:00","id":1181362,"title":"","content":"This is stuff I got from reading the world a lot and going inbetween the lines, not really stuff that I decided to change up, but It's controversial none the less. <br /> In times of old, the changing breeds were supermen who could have everything. They were powerful, and lived exceptionally good lives being able to murder/fuck anything they wanted. That's not to say that was all they did, they were very keen on family and the like, and were largely above average people with access to a power fantasy. Their only serious rivals were others of their kind, and as half spirits who could travel that world, they forged pacts and alliances with spirits to give themselves and their allies advantages over others (during these conflicts, each changer carved out the rolls of it's breed to reflect what and how they did things). Over time, this spiritual interference caused an imbalance, and the world started to change. Human civilisation started to grow , species died out, geography changed, the changers had made a mess in the name of helping spirits. When they realised their errors or the errors of others, they reacted badly, and wars between changers only got worse. They got it into their heads that they were keeping the balance, as they tried to fix wounds with amputations. <br /> <br /> Of course, the weaver rose during this (very long) period, and the wyrm eventually went mad. Banes rose more, either to deal with the weaver or as a reflection of the turbulent times. Balanced spirits, or gaian spirits, who had really caused much of the inbalance by using the changers in their own interest, were always fearful of the wyrmish spirits that meant them harm. Thus, they rallied the changers against the wyrm, promising new and stronger gifts. The wyrm, under this assault, went more and more mad, more vile and aggressive, this in turn unified many of the changers against it. Over generations many believed their purpose was to fight the wyrm, a lie encouraged by &quot;gaian&quot; spirits and the changer's own propensity for bullshit. <br /> <br /> One tribe of garou, the white howlers, known for their closeness with kin, their savagery, and their propensity for death spirits, and lion being an aloof totem, had many reasons to fall, but it's not so easy to just lose a tribe. Rather than the doomed hell charge most other garou envision, the howlers fell for their cynicism. They knew they were more loyal to themselves than to spirits, they knew their infighting created the wyrm, but they were curious as to why banes and formori came to their land; surely it was balanced in the ways of the triat and the wyrm need not send it's minions? After a time, their theurges determined that the wyrm was sick, unstable, and that it needed help, not only would the banes not ravage the land; the wyrm spirits would no doubt reward them. Most all went down to deal with the situation, some were tricked, but they didn't imagine the intensity of the wyrm's problem, with their new warped outlook, they dragged the rest of the tribe down with them. <br /> <br /> the other tribes continue on into the modern era, for the most part glued to the lies of a million years. Their infighting subdued by their duty, but the vestiges of their original nature die hard, they remain territorial, jealous, bigoted, and of course are filled with rage. Mixed septs have a tense power balance, and duels and other infights continue to kill garou despite the threat of the wyrm. The litany is the law of the garou, but it's age pales in comparison to those lawless times, and it is constantly being strained. Glass walkers are disliked for their skewed spiritual allegiances. Ronin are hounded by gaian garou because the spirits resent their lack of control. In the end, Garou are fools of their own design, and the truth is worth a silver death.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Be correct.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23728-pewpew","name":"PewPew","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"107"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-02T12:36:11-08:00","id":1181756,"title":"","content":"In my games, Black Dog Games Factory is primarily known for their Tailspinner System and &quot;Cynical Macabre&quot; World of Shadows setting, with it's primary games being Darkling: The Thirst, Changeling: The Seduction and Witchling: The Power. <br /> <br /> (I got the names from Yasmine Galenorm's Sisters of the Moon trilogy, which I've never read, but saw the three titles and thought &quot;that'd be cool names for a series of RPGs&quot; and decided to use them for this, as I prefer my PENTEX to not be quite so on-the-nose with it's parodies.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}